window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b233-7e492007e7f67857.json"]={sha256:"7e492007e7f67857955ace801f3cb6b18a5871c90282f43b4c8f96460dcc9ff7",value:{"id":"b233","title":"雙曲拱壩拱座分析","titleEn":"Abutment analysis for double-curvature arch dams","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"本課以雙曲拱壩拱座分析為入口，深入拱推力、岸坡楔體與壩岩相容的三維判讀。十個單元各自對應不同的荷載路徑、能量交換或監測問題，從守恆式建立量化估算，再檢查量測配置是否能辨認真正失效原因。工程史實只採用列明範圍的公開一手資料；所有模型輸入另標為教學假設，成果是可追溯的工程判讀紀錄。","summaryEn":"Using Abutment analysis for double-curvature arch dams as its entry point, this course examines three-dimensional interpretation of arch thrust, abutment wedges and dam-rock compatibility. Ten units address different load paths, energy exchanges or monitoring questions, starting with conservation-based estimates and testing whether observations distinguish failure causes. Historical statements use scoped primary evidence. Numerical model inputs are separately identified as teaching assumptions, producing a traceable engineering interpretation record.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-systems","subcategoryTitle":"防潮、航運與大壩施工","subcategoryTitleEn":"Tidal barriers, navigation and dam construction","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-systems","learningTags":["water","water-systems","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-dam","architectureNodes":[["薄拱膜力初估","Thin-arch membrane estimate"],["岸坡推力方向","Abutment thrust direction"],["裂隙水壓分布","Joint water-pressure distribution"],["封拱溫度與接縫閉合","Closure temperature and joint closure"],["水溫荷載與監測殘差","Hydrothermal effects and monitoring residuals"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]],"diagram":{"type":"water-dam","labels":["薄拱膜力初估","岸坡推力方向","裂隙水壓分布","封拱溫度與接縫閉合","水溫荷載與監測殘差"],"labelsEn":["Thin-arch membrane estimate","Abutment thrust direction","Joint water-pressure distribution","Closure temperature and joint closure","Hydrothermal effects and monitoring residuals"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"本課原創比較練習分兩個相互獨立的物理模型。教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設均勻徑向壓力0.5 MPa、半徑80 m、厚8 m，薄拱壓應力pR/t=5 MPa；無彎曲且理想連續圓拱。教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設兩平行線性路徑剛度ka=3 GN/m、kc=2 GN/m，共受10 MN，位移2 mm，拱分6 MN、懸臂分4 MN；僅教學彈簧類比。先逐一圈出公式內的控制體、力方向或時間尺度，再把每項輸入的量綱換成一致單位。第二人只根據輸入重算結果，不抄第一人的中間數字。最後指出這兩個估算尚未包含的空間變化、非線性及量測誤差；若將結果用於另一座工程，必須重建其幾何、材料與邊界條件，不能挪用本練習的假設。 薄拱公式的局部敏感度固定均勻徑向壓力0.5 MPa和半徑80 m，只將厚度由8增加至10 m。理想壓應力σ=pR/t由5降至4 MPa，減少20%。比較保持無彎曲的連續圓拱假設；真實加厚會改變三維剛度、溫度與拱梁分載，不能把此倒數關係視為完整拱壩設計結論。","textEn":"This original comparison exercise uses two independent physical models. Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume uniform radial pressure 0.5 MPa, radius 80 m and thickness 8 m. Thin-arch compressive stress pR/t=5 MPa, for a continuous circular arch without bending. Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume parallel linear paths ka=3 GN/m and kc=2 GN/m under total 10 MN. Displacement is 2 mm, with arch share 6 MN and cantilever share 4 MN, a spring analogy only. First identify the control volume, force direction or time scale in each relation, then convert every input to consistent units. A second reviewer recalculates from the inputs without copying intermediate numbers. Finally identify spatial variability, nonlinear effects and measurement errors omitted by both estimates. Transfer to another structure requires rebuilding its geometry, material description and boundary conditions; the assumed classroom inputs are not transferable design or operating parameters. For local sensitivity of the thin-arch relation, hold uniform radial pressure 0.5 MPa and radius 80 m fixed, increasing only thickness from 8 m to 10 m. Ideal compression σ=pR/t falls from 5 to 4 MPa, a 20% reduction. The comparison retains a continuous circular arch without bending; actual thickening changes three-dimensional stiffness, temperature and arch-cantilever sharing, so the inverse relation is not a complete dam-design conclusion.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b233-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「薄拱膜力初估」與「拱與懸臂分擔」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Thin-arch membrane estimate\" and \"Arch and cantilever load sharing\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b233-v15-01","title":"薄拱膜力初估：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Thin-arch membrane estimate: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「薄拱膜力初估」如何影響雙曲拱壩拱座分析的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Thin-arch membrane estimate” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Abutment analysis for double-curvature arch dams”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"雙曲拱壩把水壓經曲率傳向兩岸，薄圓拱膜力能提供第一個量級估算。真實壩體同時有懸臂彎曲、變厚與非圓形幾何，不能只用單一半徑設計。 假設均勻徑向壓力0.5 MPa、半徑80 m、厚8 m，薄拱壓應力pR/t=5 MPa；無彎曲且理想連續圓拱。 薄拱公式不反映接縫張開或基礎變形，局部拉應力可能在平均壓應力下仍出現。若只看整體平均壓力，會錯過岸坡傳力不均與彎曲集中。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「薄拱膜力初估」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A double-curvature arch dam transfers pressure toward the banks through curvature. Thin circular-arch membrane action gives an initial scale, while real dams also have cantilever bending, variable thickness and noncircular geometry. Assume uniform radial pressure 0.5 MPa, radius 80 m and thickness 8 m. Thin-arch compressive stress pR/t=5 MPa, for a continuous circular arch without bending. The thin-arch relation omits joint opening and foundation deformation, allowing local tension despite mean compression. Overall average stress can therefore conceal uneven abutment transfer and concentrated bending. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Thin-arch membrane estimate” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設均勻徑向壓力0.5 MPa、半徑80 m、厚8 m，薄拱壓應力pR/t=5 MPa；無彎曲且理想連續圓拱。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume uniform radial pressure 0.5 MPa, radius 80 m and thickness 8 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「薄拱平均壓應力足夠低就證明整座雙曲拱壩沒有拉應力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Low mean thin-arch compression proves there is no tensile stress anywhere in the dam.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「薄拱膜力初估」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Thin-arch membrane estimate”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b233-v15-01-k1","title":"薄拱膜力初估","titleEn":"Thin-arch membrane estimate","text":"雙曲拱壩把水壓經曲率傳向兩岸，薄圓拱膜力能提供第一個量級估算。真實壩體同時有懸臂彎曲、變厚與非圓形幾何，不能只用單一半徑設計。","textEn":"A double-curvature arch dam transfers pressure toward the banks through curvature. Thin circular-arch membrane action gives an initial scale, while real dams also have cantilever bending, variable thickness and noncircular geometry.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b233-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：薄拱平均壓應力足夠低就證明整座雙曲拱壩沒有拉應力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Low mean thin-arch compression proves there is no tensile stress anywhere in the dam. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「薄拱膜力初估」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Thin-arch membrane estimate\" is correct?","options":["薄拱平均壓應力足夠低就證明整座雙曲拱壩沒有拉應力。","雙曲拱壩把水壓經曲率傳向兩岸，薄圓拱膜力能提供第一個量級估算。","拱和懸臂的荷載比例可以任意指定而不影響位移相容。"],"optionsEn":["Low mean thin-arch compression proves there is no tensile stress anywhere in the dam.","A double-curvature arch dam transfers pressure toward the banks through curvature.","Arch and cantilever shares can be chosen arbitrarily without affecting displacement compatibility."],"answer":1,"explanation":"雙曲拱壩把水壓經曲率傳向兩岸，薄圓拱膜力能提供第一個量級估算。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A double-curvature arch dam transfers pressure toward the banks through curvature. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b233-v15-02","title":"薄拱膜力初估：定量估算","titleEn":"Thin-arch membrane estimate: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b233-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「薄拱膜力初估」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Thin-arch membrane estimate” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設均勻徑向壓力0.5 MPa、半徑80 m、厚8 m，薄拱壓應力pR/t=5 MPa；無彎曲且理想連續圓拱。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume uniform radial pressure 0.5 MPa, radius 80 m and thickness 8 m. Thin-arch compressive stress pR/t=5 MPa, for a continuous circular arch without bending. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：從各高程截面量取曲率與厚度，對照壓力分布和應變方向；將薄拱估算與含懸臂作用模型比較，查最大的偏差位置是否接近岸坡或幾何轉折。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure curvature and thickness at several elevations and compare pressure and strain directions.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b233-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設均勻徑向壓力0.5 MPa、半徑80 m、厚8 m，薄拱壓應力pR/t=5 MPa；無彎曲且理想連續圓拱。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume uniform radial pressure 0.5 MPa, radius 80 m and thickness 8 m. Thin-arch compressive stress pR/t=5 MPa, for a continuous circular arch without bending.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b233-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「薄拱膜力初估」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Thin-arch membrane estimate\", which statement holds?","options":["岩石單軸強度很高就能排除沿節理滑動的岸坡失穩。","完整岩芯彈性模數可以無條件等同整個節理岩體模數。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設均勻徑向壓力0.5 MPa、半徑80 m、厚8 m，薄拱壓應力pR/t=5 MPa；無彎曲且理想連續圓拱。"],"optionsEn":["High intact-rock compressive strength rules out abutment failure by joint sliding.","Intact-core elastic modulus can unconditionally represent the entire jointed rock mass.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume uniform radial pressure 0.5 MPa, radius 80 m and thickness 8 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設均勻徑向壓力0.5 MPa、半徑80 m、厚8 m，薄拱壓應力pR/t=5 MPa；無彎曲且理想連續圓拱。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume uniform radial pressure 0.5 MPa, radius 80 m and thickness 8 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b233-v15-03","title":"薄拱膜力初估：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Thin-arch membrane estimate: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b233-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「薄拱膜力初估」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Thin-arch membrane estimate” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"從各高程截面量取曲率與厚度，對照壓力分布和應變方向；將薄拱估算與含懸臂作用模型比較，查最大的偏差位置是否接近岸坡或幾何轉折。分開報告拱冠與拱座附近的彎曲應力。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure curvature and thickness at several elevations and compare pressure and strain directions. Contrast the membrane estimate with a model including cantilever action, locating deviations near abutments or geometric transitions. Report bending stresses near the crown and abutments as separate quantities. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以薄拱膜力初估編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。從各高程截面量取曲率與厚度，對照壓力分布和應變方向；將薄拱估算與含懸臂作用模型比較，查最大的偏差位置是否接近岸坡或幾何轉折。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for thin-arch membrane estimate, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Measure curvature and thickness at several elevations and compare pressure and strain directions. Contrast the membrane estimate with a model including cantilever action, locating deviations near abutments or geometric transitions.","failure":"注意干擾：薄拱公式不反映接縫張開或基礎變形，局部拉應力可能在平均壓應力下仍出現。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: The thin-arch relation omits joint opening and foundation deformation, allowing local tension despite mean compression. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b233-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"從各高程截面量取曲率與厚度，對照壓力分布和應變方向；將薄拱估算與含懸臂作用模型比較，查最大的偏差位置是否接近岸坡或幾何轉折。分開報告拱冠與拱座附近的彎曲應力。","textEn":"Measure curvature and thickness at several elevations and compare pressure and strain directions. Contrast the membrane estimate with a model including cantilever action, locating deviations near abutments or geometric transitions. Report bending stresses near the crown and abutments as separate quantities.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b233-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以薄拱膜力初估編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。從各高程截面量取曲率與厚度，對照壓力分布和應變方向；將薄拱估算與含懸臂作用模型比較，查最大的偏差位置是否接近岸坡或幾何轉折。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for thin-arch membrane estimate, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Measure curvature and thickness at several elevations and compare pressure and strain directions. Contrast the membrane estimate with a model including cantilever action, locating deviations near abutments or geometric transitions.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「薄拱膜力初估」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Thin-arch membrane estimate\"?","options":["從各高程截面量取曲率與厚度，對照壓力分布和應變方向；將薄拱估算與含懸臂作用模型比較，查最大的偏差位置是否接近岸坡或幾何轉折。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","壩頂位移收斂就能證明所有局部最大應力都已收斂。"],"optionsEn":["Measure curvature and thickness at several elevations and compare pressure and strain directions.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Converged crest displacement proves convergence of every local maximum stress."],"answer":0,"explanation":"從各高程截面量取曲率與厚度，對照壓力分布和應變方向；將薄拱估算與含懸臂作用模型比較，查最大的偏差位置是否接近岸坡或幾何轉折。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure curvature and thickness at several elevations and compare pressure and strain directions. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b233-v15-04","title":"薄拱膜力初估：失效診斷","titleEn":"Thin-arch membrane estimate: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b233-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「薄拱膜力初估」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Thin-arch membrane estimate” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"薄拱公式不反映接縫張開或基礎變形，局部拉應力可能在平均壓應力下仍出現。若只看整體平均壓力，會錯過岸坡傳力不均與彎曲集中。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"The thin-arch relation omits joint opening and foundation deformation, allowing local tension despite mean compression. Overall average stress can therefore conceal uneven abutment transfer and concentrated bending. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：若只看整體平均壓力，會錯過岸坡傳力不均與彎曲集中。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Overall average stress can therefore conceal uneven abutment transfer and concentrated bending.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「薄拱平均壓應力足夠低就證明整座雙曲拱壩沒有拉應力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Low mean thin-arch compression proves there is no tensile stress anywhere in the dam.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b233-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"薄拱公式不反映接縫張開或基礎變形，局部拉應力可能在平均壓應力下仍出現。若只看整體平均壓力，會錯過岸坡傳力不均與彎曲集中。","textEn":"The thin-arch relation omits joint opening and foundation deformation, allowing local tension despite mean compression. Overall average stress can therefore conceal uneven abutment transfer and concentrated bending.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b233-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「薄拱膜力初估」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Thin-arch membrane estimate\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","薄拱公式不反映接縫張開或基礎變形，局部拉應力可能在平均壓應力下仍出現。","拱和懸臂的荷載比例可以任意指定而不影響位移相容。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","The thin-arch relation omits joint opening and foundation deformation, allowing local tension despite mean compression.","Arch and cantilever shares can be chosen arbitrarily without affecting displacement compatibility."],"answer":1,"explanation":"薄拱公式不反映接縫張開或基礎變形，局部拉應力可能在平均壓應力下仍出現。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"The thin-arch relation omits joint opening and foundation deformation, allowing local tension despite mean compression. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b233-v15-05","title":"拱與懸臂分擔：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Arch and cantilever load sharing: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b233-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「拱與懸臂分擔」如何影響雙曲拱壩拱座分析的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Arch and cantilever load sharing” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Abutment analysis for double-curvature arch dams”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"壩體可由水平拱與豎向懸臂共同分擔水壓，兩者變形必須相容。分擔比例由剛度與邊界形成，不是可任意指定以降低應力的設計選項。 假設兩平行線性路徑剛度ka=3 GN/m、kc=2 GN/m，共受10 MN，位移2 mm，拱分6 MN、懸臂分4 MN；僅教學彈簧類比。 一條路徑剛度被高估會把荷載過度導向該路徑，整體平衡仍可能成立。只校準壩頂位移而忽略局部應變，可能得到錯誤卻看似吻合的內力分配。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「拱與懸臂分擔」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Horizontal arches and vertical cantilevers share pressure while maintaining compatible movement. Relative stiffness and boundaries determine sharing; the proportions cannot be arbitrarily chosen to make stresses smaller. Assume parallel linear paths ka=3 GN/m and kc=2 GN/m under total 10 MN. Displacement is 2 mm, with arch share 6 MN and cantilever share 4 MN, a spring analogy only. Overstated stiffness attracts too much load to one path even while global equilibrium holds. Calibrating only crest displacement can produce a misleadingly good fit with incorrect local force distribution. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Arch and cantilever load sharing” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設兩平行線性路徑剛度ka=3 GN/m、kc=2 GN/m，共受10 MN，位移2 mm，拱分6 MN、懸臂分4 MN；僅教學彈簧類比。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume parallel linear paths ka=3 GN/m and kc=2 GN/m under total 10 MN.","failure":"常見誤解：「拱和懸臂的荷載比例可以任意指定而不影響位移相容。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Arch and cantilever shares can be chosen arbitrarily without affecting displacement compatibility.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「拱與懸臂分擔」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Arch and cantilever load sharing”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b233-v15-05-k1","title":"拱與懸臂分擔","titleEn":"Arch and cantilever load sharing","text":"壩體可由水平拱與豎向懸臂共同分擔水壓，兩者變形必須相容。分擔比例由剛度與邊界形成，不是可任意指定以降低應力的設計選項。","textEn":"Horizontal arches and vertical cantilevers share pressure while maintaining compatible movement. Relative stiffness and boundaries determine sharing; the proportions cannot be arbitrarily chosen to make stresses smaller.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b233-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：拱和懸臂的荷載比例可以任意指定而不影響位移相容。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Arch and cantilever shares can be chosen arbitrarily without affecting displacement compatibility. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「拱與懸臂分擔」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Arch and cantilever load sharing\" is correct?","options":["拱和懸臂的荷載比例可以任意指定而不影響位移相容。","岸坡承受的總推力越大就必定越穩定，方向不重要。","壩體可由水平拱與豎向懸臂共同分擔水壓，兩者變形必須相容。"],"optionsEn":["Arch and cantilever shares can be chosen arbitrarily without affecting displacement compatibility.","Greater total abutment thrust always improves stability regardless of its direction.","Horizontal arches and vertical cantilevers share pressure while maintaining compatible movement."],"answer":2,"explanation":"壩體可由水平拱與豎向懸臂共同分擔水壓，兩者變形必須相容。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Horizontal arches and vertical cantilevers share pressure while maintaining compatible movement. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b233-v15-06","title":"拱與懸臂分擔：定量估算","titleEn":"Arch and cantilever load sharing: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b233-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「拱與懸臂分擔」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Arch and cantilever load sharing” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設兩平行線性路徑剛度ka=3 GN/m、kc=2 GN/m，共受10 MN，位移2 mm，拱分6 MN、懸臂分4 MN；僅教學彈簧類比。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume parallel linear paths ka=3 GN/m and kc=2 GN/m under total 10 MN. Displacement is 2 mm, with arch share 6 MN and cantilever share 4 MN, a spring analogy only. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對兩路徑在交點的位移相容及合力平衡，改變壩岩剛度做敏感度；將簡化分擔與三維位移和應變結果比較，避免只追求總反力正確。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check displacement compatibility and force balance at shared points and vary dam-rock stiffness.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b233-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設兩平行線性路徑剛度ka=3 GN/m、kc=2 GN/m，共受10 MN，位移2 mm，拱分6 MN、懸臂分4 MN；僅教學彈簧類比。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume parallel linear paths ka=3 GN/m and kc=2 GN/m under total 10 MN. Displacement is 2 mm, with arch share 6 MN and cantilever share 4 MN, a spring analogy only.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b233-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「拱與懸臂分擔」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Arch and cantilever load sharing\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設兩平行線性路徑剛度ka=3 GN/m、kc=2 GN/m，共受10 MN，位移2 mm，拱分6 MN、懸臂分4 MN。","裂隙出水很少就能證明整個岸坡節理水壓很低。","接縫灌漿溫度只影響施工方便，不影響後續拱壩受力。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume parallel linear paths ka=3 GN/m and kc=2 GN/m under total 10 MN.","Small joint discharge proves low water pressure throughout all abutment discontinuities.","Joint-grouting temperature affects convenience only and not later arch-dam structural behavior."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設兩平行線性路徑剛度ka=3 GN/m、kc=2 GN/m，共受10 MN，位移2 mm，拱分6 MN、懸臂分4 MN；僅教學彈簧類比。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume parallel linear paths ka=3 GN/m and kc=2 GN/m under total 10 MN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b233-v15-07","title":"拱與懸臂分擔：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Arch and cantilever load sharing: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b233-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「拱與懸臂分擔」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Arch and cantilever load sharing” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對兩路徑在交點的位移相容及合力平衡，改變壩岩剛度做敏感度；將簡化分擔與三維位移和應變結果比較，避免只追求總反力正確。確認兩路徑分擔總和仍等於原始水壓荷載。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check displacement compatibility and force balance at shared points and vary dam-rock stiffness. Compare simplified sharing with three-dimensional displacement and strain, rather than accepting a correct total reaction alone. Verify that the sum of both load paths still equals applied water loading. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以拱與懸臂分擔編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。核對兩路徑在交點的位移相容及合力平衡，改變壩岩剛度做敏感度；將簡化分擔與三維位移和應變結果比較，避免只追求總反力正確。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for arch and cantilever load sharing, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Check displacement compatibility and force balance at shared points and vary dam-rock stiffness. Compare simplified sharing with three-dimensional displacement and strain, rather than accepting a correct total reaction alone.","failure":"注意干擾：一條路徑剛度被高估會把荷載過度導向該路徑，整體平衡仍可能成立。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Overstated stiffness attracts too much load to one path even while global equilibrium holds. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b233-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對兩路徑在交點的位移相容及合力平衡，改變壩岩剛度做敏感度；將簡化分擔與三維位移和應變結果比較，避免只追求總反力正確。確認兩路徑分擔總和仍等於原始水壓荷載。","textEn":"Check displacement compatibility and force balance at shared points and vary dam-rock stiffness. Compare simplified sharing with three-dimensional displacement and strain, rather than accepting a correct total reaction alone. Verify that the sum of both load paths still equals applied water loading.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b233-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以拱與懸臂分擔編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。核對兩路徑在交點的位移相容及合力平衡，改變壩岩剛度做敏感度；將簡化分擔與三維位移和應變結果比較，避免只追求總反力正確。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for arch and cantilever load sharing, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Check displacement compatibility and force balance at shared points and vary dam-rock stiffness. Compare simplified sharing with three-dimensional displacement and strain, rather than accepting a correct total reaction alone.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「拱與懸臂分擔」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Arch and cantilever load sharing\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","核對兩路徑在交點的位移相容及合力平衡，改變壩岩剛度做敏感度；將簡化分擔與三維位移和應變結果比較，避免只追求總反力正確。","把峰值地面加速度乘壩重就能完整代表三維地震反應。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Check displacement compatibility and force balance at shared points and vary dam-rock stiffness.","Peak ground acceleration times dam weight completely represents three-dimensional earthquake response."],"answer":1,"explanation":"核對兩路徑在交點的位移相容及合力平衡，改變壩岩剛度做敏感度；將簡化分擔與三維位移和應變結果比較，避免只追求總反力正確。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check displacement compatibility and force balance at shared points and vary dam-rock stiffness. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b233-v15-08","title":"拱與懸臂分擔：失效診斷","titleEn":"Arch and cantilever load sharing: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b233-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「拱與懸臂分擔」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Arch and cantilever load sharing” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"一條路徑剛度被高估會把荷載過度導向該路徑，整體平衡仍可能成立。只校準壩頂位移而忽略局部應變，可能得到錯誤卻看似吻合的內力分配。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Overstated stiffness attracts too much load to one path even while global equilibrium holds. Calibrating only crest displacement can produce a misleadingly good fit with incorrect local force distribution. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：只校準壩頂位移而忽略局部應變，可能得到錯誤卻看似吻合的內力分配。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Calibrating only crest displacement can produce a misleadingly good fit with incorrect local force distribution.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「拱和懸臂的荷載比例可以任意指定而不影響位移相容。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Arch and cantilever shares can be chosen arbitrarily without affecting displacement compatibility.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b233-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"一條路徑剛度被高估會把荷載過度導向該路徑，整體平衡仍可能成立。只校準壩頂位移而忽略局部應變，可能得到錯誤卻看似吻合的內力分配。","textEn":"Overstated stiffness attracts too much load to one path even while global equilibrium holds. Calibrating only crest displacement can produce a misleadingly good fit with incorrect local force distribution.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b233-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「拱與懸臂分擔」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Arch and cantilever load sharing\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","岸坡承受的總推力越大就必定越穩定，方向不重要。","一條路徑剛度被高估會把荷載過度導向該路徑，整體平衡仍可能成立。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Greater total abutment thrust always improves stability regardless of its direction.","Overstated stiffness attracts too much load to one path even while global equilibrium holds."],"answer":2,"explanation":"一條路徑剛度被高估會把荷載過度導向該路徑，整體平衡仍可能成立。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Overstated stiffness attracts too much load to one path even while global equilibrium holds. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b233-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「岸坡推力方向」與「楔體滑動抗力」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Abutment thrust direction\" and \"Wedge sliding resistance\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b233-v15-09","title":"岸坡推力方向：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Abutment thrust direction: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b233-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「岸坡推力方向」如何影響雙曲拱壩拱座分析的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Abutment thrust direction” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Abutment analysis for double-curvature arch dams”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"拱推力到達岸坡時需要分解到岩面法向與剪向，方向與大小同樣重要。大壓力若指向易滑節理組合，仍可能形成不利楔體受力。 假設推力20 MN與岩面法向夾角30°，法向17.3205 MN、剪向10 MN；平面向量示例，不代表三維楔體完整力系。 角度定義混淆會交換法向與剪向分量，直接改變摩擦判讀。若把整個岸坡用單一平面代表，可能漏掉由兩組節理交線控制的三維運動方向。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「岸坡推力方向」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Arch thrust must be resolved normal and tangential to abutment surfaces, making direction as important as magnitude. Large compression can still destabilize a wedge when directed unfavorably relative to joints. Assume thrust 20 MN at thirty degrees to the rock-surface normal. Normal component is 17.3205 MN and tangential component 10 MN, a planar illustration rather than a complete wedge force system. Confusing angle definitions swaps normal and tangential components and changes friction assessment. Representing the whole abutment by one plane can miss three-dimensional movement controlled by intersecting joint sets. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Abutment thrust direction” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設推力20 MN與岩面法向夾角30°，法向17.3205 MN、剪向10 MN；平面向量示例，不代表三維楔體完整力系。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume thrust 20 MN at thirty degrees to the rock-surface normal.","failure":"常見誤解：「岸坡承受的總推力越大就必定越穩定，方向不重要。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Greater total abutment thrust always improves stability regardless of its direction.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「岸坡推力方向」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Abutment thrust direction”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b233-v15-09-k1","title":"岸坡推力方向","titleEn":"Abutment thrust direction","text":"拱推力到達岸坡時需要分解到岩面法向與剪向，方向與大小同樣重要。大壓力若指向易滑節理組合，仍可能形成不利楔體受力。","textEn":"Arch thrust must be resolved normal and tangential to abutment surfaces, making direction as important as magnitude. Large compression can still destabilize a wedge when directed unfavorably relative to joints.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b233-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：岸坡承受的總推力越大就必定越穩定，方向不重要。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Greater total abutment thrust always improves stability regardless of its direction. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「岸坡推力方向」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Abutment thrust direction\" is correct?","options":["拱推力到達岸坡時需要分解到岩面法向與剪向，方向與大小同樣重要。","岸坡承受的總推力越大就必定越穩定，方向不重要。","岩石單軸強度很高就能排除沿節理滑動的岸坡失穩。"],"optionsEn":["Arch thrust must be resolved normal and tangential to abutment surfaces, making direction as important as magnitude.","Greater total abutment thrust always improves stability regardless of its direction.","High intact-rock compressive strength rules out abutment failure by joint sliding."],"answer":0,"explanation":"拱推力到達岸坡時需要分解到岩面法向與剪向，方向與大小同樣重要。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Arch thrust must be resolved normal and tangential to abutment surfaces, making direction as important as magnitude. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b233-v15-10","title":"岸坡推力方向：定量估算","titleEn":"Abutment thrust direction: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b233-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「岸坡推力方向」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Abutment thrust direction” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設推力20 MN與岩面法向夾角30°，法向17.3205 MN、剪向10 MN；平面向量示例，不代表三維楔體完整力系。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume thrust 20 MN at thirty degrees to the rock-surface normal. Normal component is 17.3205 MN and tangential component 10 MN, a planar illustration rather than a complete wedge force system. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：把節理法向和推力向量放到同一座標系，核對角度是相對法向還是面本身；用測繪和模型反力交叉確認，並保留各高程推力方向變化。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Put joint normals and thrust in a common coordinate system and verify whether angles reference normals or surfaces.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b233-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設推力20 MN與岩面法向夾角30°，法向17.3205 MN、剪向10 MN；平面向量示例，不代表三維楔體完整力系。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume thrust 20 MN at thirty degrees to the rock-surface normal. Normal component is 17.3205 MN and tangential component 10 MN, a planar illustration rather than a complete wedge force system.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b233-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「岸坡推力方向」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Abutment thrust direction\", which statement holds?","options":["完整岩芯彈性模數可以無條件等同整個節理岩體模數。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設推力20 MN與岩面法向夾角30°，法向17.3205 MN、剪向10 MN；平面向量示例，不代表三維楔體完整力系。","壩頂位移收斂就能證明所有局部最大應力都已收斂。"],"optionsEn":["Intact-core elastic modulus can unconditionally represent the entire jointed rock mass.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume thrust 20 MN at thirty degrees to the rock-surface normal.","Converged crest displacement proves convergence of every local maximum stress."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設推力20 MN與岩面法向夾角30°，法向17.3205 MN、剪向10 MN；平面向量示例，不代表三維楔體完整力系。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume thrust 20 MN at thirty degrees to the rock-surface normal. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b233-v15-11","title":"岸坡推力方向：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Abutment thrust direction: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b233-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「岸坡推力方向」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Abutment thrust direction” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"把節理法向和推力向量放到同一座標系，核對角度是相對法向還是面本身；用測繪和模型反力交叉確認，並保留各高程推力方向變化。以向量點積獨立重算法向與剪向分量。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Put joint normals and thrust in a common coordinate system and verify whether angles reference normals or surfaces. Cross-check mapping and model reactions, retaining changes in thrust direction with elevation. Independently recompute normal and tangential components using vector projections. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以岸坡推力方向編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。把節理法向和推力向量放到同一座標系，核對角度是相對法向還是面本身；用測繪和模型反力交叉確認，並保留各高程推力方向變化。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for abutment thrust direction, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Put joint normals and thrust in a common coordinate system and verify whether angles reference normals or surfaces. Cross-check mapping and model reactions, retaining changes in thrust direction with elevation.","failure":"注意干擾：角度定義混淆會交換法向與剪向分量，直接改變摩擦判讀。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Confusing angle definitions swaps normal and tangential components and changes friction assessment. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b233-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"把節理法向和推力向量放到同一座標系，核對角度是相對法向還是面本身；用測繪和模型反力交叉確認，並保留各高程推力方向變化。以向量點積獨立重算法向與剪向分量。","textEn":"Put joint normals and thrust in a common coordinate system and verify whether angles reference normals or surfaces. Cross-check mapping and model reactions, retaining changes in thrust direction with elevation. Independently recompute normal and tangential components using vector projections.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b233-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以岸坡推力方向編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。把節理法向和推力向量放到同一座標系，核對角度是相對法向還是面本身；用測繪和模型反力交叉確認，並保留各高程推力方向變化。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for abutment thrust direction, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Put joint normals and thrust in a common coordinate system and verify whether angles reference normals or surfaces. Cross-check mapping and model reactions, retaining changes in thrust direction with elevation.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「岸坡推力方向」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Abutment thrust direction\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","只要重新擬合後殘差變小，就證明原先結構異常已消失。","把節理法向和推力向量放到同一座標系，核對角度是相對法向還是面本身；用測繪和模型反力交叉確認，並保留各高程推力方向變化。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","A smaller residual after refitting proves the original structural anomaly has disappeared.","Put joint normals and thrust in a common coordinate system and verify whether angles reference normals or surfaces."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把節理法向和推力向量放到同一座標系，核對角度是相對法向還是面本身；用測繪和模型反力交叉確認，並保留各高程推力方向變化。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Put joint normals and thrust in a common coordinate system and verify whether angles reference normals or surfaces. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b233-v15-12","title":"岸坡推力方向：失效診斷","titleEn":"Abutment thrust direction: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b233-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「岸坡推力方向」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Abutment thrust direction” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"角度定義混淆會交換法向與剪向分量，直接改變摩擦判讀。若把整個岸坡用單一平面代表，可能漏掉由兩組節理交線控制的三維運動方向。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Confusing angle definitions swaps normal and tangential components and changes friction assessment. Representing the whole abutment by one plane can miss three-dimensional movement controlled by intersecting joint sets. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：若把整個岸坡用單一平面代表，可能漏掉由兩組節理交線控制的三維運動方向。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Representing the whole abutment by one plane can miss three-dimensional movement controlled by intersecting joint sets.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「岸坡承受的總推力越大就必定越穩定，方向不重要。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Greater total abutment thrust always improves stability regardless of its direction.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b233-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"角度定義混淆會交換法向與剪向分量，直接改變摩擦判讀。若把整個岸坡用單一平面代表，可能漏掉由兩組節理交線控制的三維運動方向。","textEn":"Confusing angle definitions swaps normal and tangential components and changes friction assessment. Representing the whole abutment by one plane can miss three-dimensional movement controlled by intersecting joint sets.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b233-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「岸坡推力方向」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Abutment thrust direction\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["角度定義混淆會交換法向與剪向分量，直接改變摩擦判讀。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","岩石單軸強度很高就能排除沿節理滑動的岸坡失穩。"],"optionsEn":["Confusing angle definitions swaps normal and tangential components and changes friction assessment.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","High intact-rock compressive strength rules out abutment failure by joint sliding."],"answer":0,"explanation":"角度定義混淆會交換法向與剪向分量，直接改變摩擦判讀。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Confusing angle definitions swaps normal and tangential components and changes friction assessment. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b233-v15-13","title":"楔體滑動抗力：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Wedge sliding resistance: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b233-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「楔體滑動抗力」如何影響雙曲拱壩拱座分析的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Wedge sliding resistance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Abutment analysis for double-curvature arch dams”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"岸坡不穩定可能沿既有節理滑動，而非岩石材料壓碎。有效正向力、節理摩擦與水壓控制抗力，幾何可動性必須先於數值安全比判讀。 假設單滑面總正力30 MN、水壓合力8 MN、摩擦角35°、驅動剪力10 MN，無黏聚比值(30−8)tan35°/10=1.5405。 即使岩石單軸強度高，光滑充填節理仍可能具有低抗剪。若忽略節理水壓或錯將不連續面當完整岩體，會高估岸坡承載並錯估壩體反力邊界。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「楔體滑動抗力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Abutments can fail by sliding on existing joints rather than crushing intact rock. Effective normal force, joint friction and water pressure govern resistance, after geometric freedom to move has been established. Assume single-plane normal force 30 MN, water resultant 8 MN, friction angle 35 degrees and driving shear 10 MN. Cohesionless resistance ratio is 1.5405. Strong intact rock can contain smooth filled joints with low shear resistance. Omitting joint pressure or treating discontinuities as intact material overstates abutment support and distorts the boundary reactions assigned to the dam. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Wedge sliding resistance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設單滑面總正力30 MN、水壓合力8 MN、摩擦角35°、驅動剪力10 MN，無黏聚比值(30−8)tan35°/10=1.5405。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume single-plane normal force 30 MN, water resultant 8 MN, friction angle 35 degrees and driving shear 10 MN.","failure":"常見誤解：「岩石單軸強度很高就能排除沿節理滑動的岸坡失穩。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"High intact-rock compressive strength rules out abutment failure by joint sliding.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「楔體滑動抗力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Wedge sliding resistance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b233-v15-13-k1","title":"楔體滑動抗力","titleEn":"Wedge sliding resistance","text":"岸坡不穩定可能沿既有節理滑動，而非岩石材料壓碎。有效正向力、節理摩擦與水壓控制抗力，幾何可動性必須先於數值安全比判讀。","textEn":"Abutments can fail by sliding on existing joints rather than crushing intact rock. Effective normal force, joint friction and water pressure govern resistance, after geometric freedom to move has been established.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b233-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：岩石單軸強度很高就能排除沿節理滑動的岸坡失穩。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: High intact-rock compressive strength rules out abutment failure by joint sliding. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「楔體滑動抗力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Wedge sliding resistance\" is correct?","options":["岩石單軸強度很高就能排除沿節理滑動的岸坡失穩。","岸坡不穩定可能沿既有節理滑動，而非岩石材料壓碎。","裂隙出水很少就能證明整個岸坡節理水壓很低。"],"optionsEn":["High intact-rock compressive strength rules out abutment failure by joint sliding.","Abutments can fail by sliding on existing joints rather than crushing intact rock.","Small joint discharge proves low water pressure throughout all abutment discontinuities."],"answer":1,"explanation":"岸坡不穩定可能沿既有節理滑動，而非岩石材料壓碎。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Abutments can fail by sliding on existing joints rather than crushing intact rock. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b233-v15-14","title":"楔體滑動抗力：定量估算","titleEn":"Wedge sliding resistance: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b233-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「楔體滑動抗力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Wedge sliding resistance” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設單滑面總正力30 MN、水壓合力8 MN、摩擦角35°、驅動剪力10 MN，無黏聚比值(30−8)tan35°/10=1.5405。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume single-plane normal force 30 MN, water resultant 8 MN, friction angle 35 degrees and driving shear 10 MN. Cohesionless resistance ratio is 1.5405. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用節理測繪確認滑面連續性和出露，將孔壓位置與實際滑面對應；分開峰值與殘餘摩擦，檢查楔體位移及裂縫監測是否支持所假設運動模式。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Map continuity and daylighting of the sliding surface and locate pore pressures relative to it.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b233-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設單滑面總正力30 MN、水壓合力8 MN、摩擦角35°、驅動剪力10 MN，無黏聚比值(30−8)tan35°/10=1.5405。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume single-plane normal force 30 MN, water resultant 8 MN, friction angle 35 degrees and driving shear 10 MN. Cohesionless resistance ratio is 1.5405.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b233-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「楔體滑動抗力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Wedge sliding resistance\", which statement holds?","options":["接縫灌漿溫度只影響施工方便，不影響後續拱壩受力。","把峰值地面加速度乘壩重就能完整代表三維地震反應。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設單滑面總正力30 MN、水壓合力8 MN、摩擦角35°、驅動剪力10 MN，無黏聚比值(30−8)tan35°/10=1.5405。"],"optionsEn":["Joint-grouting temperature affects convenience only and not later arch-dam structural behavior.","Peak ground acceleration times dam weight completely represents three-dimensional earthquake response.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume single-plane normal force 30 MN, water resultant 8 MN, friction angle 35 degrees and driving shear 10 MN."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設單滑面總正力30 MN、水壓合力8 MN、摩擦角35°、驅動剪力10 MN，無黏聚比值(30−8)tan35°/10=1.5405。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume single-plane normal force 30 MN, water resultant 8 MN, friction angle 35 degrees and driving shear 10 MN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b233-v15-15","title":"楔體滑動抗力：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Wedge sliding resistance: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b233-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「楔體滑動抗力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Wedge sliding resistance” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用節理測繪確認滑面連續性和出露，將孔壓位置與實際滑面對應；分開峰值與殘餘摩擦，檢查楔體位移及裂縫監測是否支持所假設運動模式。檢查潛在楔體是否真有可向外移動的自由面。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Map continuity and daylighting of the sliding surface and locate pore pressures relative to it. Separate peak and residual friction and check whether wedge movement and crack observations support the assumed mechanism. Check whether the potential wedge genuinely has an outward movement surface. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以楔體滑動抗力編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。用節理測繪確認滑面連續性和出露，將孔壓位置與實際滑面對應；分開峰值與殘餘摩擦，檢查楔體位移及裂縫監測是否支持所假設運動模式。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for wedge sliding resistance, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Map continuity and daylighting of the sliding surface and locate pore pressures relative to it. Separate peak and residual friction and check whether wedge movement and crack observations support the assumed mechanism.","failure":"注意干擾：即使岩石單軸強度高，光滑充填節理仍可能具有低抗剪。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Strong intact rock can contain smooth filled joints with low shear resistance. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b233-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用節理測繪確認滑面連續性和出露，將孔壓位置與實際滑面對應；分開峰值與殘餘摩擦，檢查楔體位移及裂縫監測是否支持所假設運動模式。檢查潛在楔體是否真有可向外移動的自由面。","textEn":"Map continuity and daylighting of the sliding surface and locate pore pressures relative to it. Separate peak and residual friction and check whether wedge movement and crack observations support the assumed mechanism. Check whether the potential wedge genuinely has an outward movement surface.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b233-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以楔體滑動抗力編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。用節理測繪確認滑面連續性和出露，將孔壓位置與實際滑面對應；分開峰值與殘餘摩擦，檢查楔體位移及裂縫監測是否支持所假設運動模式。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for wedge sliding resistance, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Map continuity and daylighting of the sliding surface and locate pore pressures relative to it. Separate peak and residual friction and check whether wedge movement and crack observations support the assumed mechanism.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「楔體滑動抗力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Wedge sliding resistance\"?","options":["用節理測繪確認滑面連續性和出露，將孔壓位置與實際滑面對應；分開峰值與殘餘摩擦，檢查楔體位移及裂縫監測是否支持所假設運動模式。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","薄拱平均壓應力足夠低就證明整座雙曲拱壩沒有拉應力。"],"optionsEn":["Map continuity and daylighting of the sliding surface and locate pore pressures relative to it.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Low mean thin-arch compression proves there is no tensile stress anywhere in the dam."],"answer":0,"explanation":"用節理測繪確認滑面連續性和出露，將孔壓位置與實際滑面對應；分開峰值與殘餘摩擦，檢查楔體位移及裂縫監測是否支持所假設運動模式。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Map continuity and daylighting of the sliding surface and locate pore pressures relative to it. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b233-v15-16","title":"楔體滑動抗力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Wedge sliding resistance: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b233-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「楔體滑動抗力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Wedge sliding resistance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"即使岩石單軸強度高，光滑充填節理仍可能具有低抗剪。若忽略節理水壓或錯將不連續面當完整岩體，會高估岸坡承載並錯估壩體反力邊界。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Strong intact rock can contain smooth filled joints with low shear resistance. Omitting joint pressure or treating discontinuities as intact material overstates abutment support and distorts the boundary reactions assigned to the dam. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：若忽略節理水壓或錯將不連續面當完整岩體，會高估岸坡承載並錯估壩體反力邊界。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Omitting joint pressure or treating discontinuities as intact material overstates abutment support and distorts the boundary reactions assigned to the dam.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「岩石單軸強度很高就能排除沿節理滑動的岸坡失穩。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"High intact-rock compressive strength rules out abutment failure by joint sliding.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b233-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"即使岩石單軸強度高，光滑充填節理仍可能具有低抗剪。若忽略節理水壓或錯將不連續面當完整岩體，會高估岸坡承載並錯估壩體反力邊界。","textEn":"Strong intact rock can contain smooth filled joints with low shear resistance. Omitting joint pressure or treating discontinuities as intact material overstates abutment support and distorts the boundary reactions assigned to the dam.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b233-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「楔體滑動抗力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Wedge sliding resistance\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","即使岩石單軸強度高，光滑充填節理仍可能具有低抗剪。","裂隙出水很少就能證明整個岸坡節理水壓很低。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Strong intact rock can contain smooth filled joints with low shear resistance.","Small joint discharge proves low water pressure throughout all abutment discontinuities."],"answer":1,"explanation":"即使岩石單軸強度高，光滑充填節理仍可能具有低抗剪。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Strong intact rock can contain smooth filled joints with low shear resistance. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b233-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「裂隙水壓分布」與「岩體柔度與拱座位移」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Joint water-pressure distribution\" and \"Rock compliance and abutment movement\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b233-v15-17","title":"裂隙水壓分布：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Joint water-pressure distribution: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b233-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「裂隙水壓分布」如何影響雙曲拱壩拱座分析的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Joint water-pressure distribution” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Abutment analysis for double-curvature arch dams”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"水沿岩體節理傳遞到岸坡內部，裂隙開度與排水會使壓力分布不同於外部庫水線性內插。水壓合力及作用點都會影響楔體穩定。 假設矩形節理面200 m²，壓力由上緣0線性增到底部0.4 MPa，水壓合力40 MN，作用點距低壓邊2/3長度；限線性分布。 出水量小可能因通道堵塞而水壓更高，不等於岸坡變乾。只用一個低壓測點代表整個滑面，會低估未排水區的合力和不利力矩。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「裂隙水壓分布」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Water transmits through abutment joints, with aperture and drainage producing pressure distributions different from a simple interpolation of reservoir level. Both resultant and location influence wedge stability. Assume joint area 200 m² with pressure rising linearly from zero to 0.4 MPa. Resultant is 40 MN at two-thirds length from the low-pressure edge, for a linear distribution. Low discharge can indicate blockage with higher pressure rather than drier rock. Extending one low-pressure point over the full slip plane understates force and adverse moment in undrained portions. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Joint water-pressure distribution” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設矩形節理面200 m²，壓力由上緣0線性增到底部0.4 MPa，水壓合力40 MN，作用點距低壓邊2/3長度；限線性分布。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume joint area 200 m² with pressure rising linearly from zero to 0.4 MPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「裂隙出水很少就能證明整個岸坡節理水壓很低。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Small joint discharge proves low water pressure throughout all abutment discontinuities.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「裂隙水壓分布」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Joint water-pressure distribution”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b233-v15-17-k1","title":"裂隙水壓分布","titleEn":"Joint water-pressure distribution","text":"水沿岩體節理傳遞到岸坡內部，裂隙開度與排水會使壓力分布不同於外部庫水線性內插。水壓合力及作用點都會影響楔體穩定。","textEn":"Water transmits through abutment joints, with aperture and drainage producing pressure distributions different from a simple interpolation of reservoir level. Both resultant and location influence wedge stability.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b233-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：裂隙出水很少就能證明整個岸坡節理水壓很低。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Small joint discharge proves low water pressure throughout all abutment discontinuities. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「裂隙水壓分布」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Joint water-pressure distribution\" is correct?","options":["裂隙出水很少就能證明整個岸坡節理水壓很低。","完整岩芯彈性模數可以無條件等同整個節理岩體模數。","水沿岩體節理傳遞到岸坡內部，裂隙開度與排水會使壓力分布不同於外部庫水線性內插。"],"optionsEn":["Small joint discharge proves low water pressure throughout all abutment discontinuities.","Intact-core elastic modulus can unconditionally represent the entire jointed rock mass.","Water transmits through abutment joints, with aperture and drainage producing pressure distributions different from a simple interpolation of reservoir level."],"answer":2,"explanation":"水沿岩體節理傳遞到岸坡內部，裂隙開度與排水會使壓力分布不同於外部庫水線性內插。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Water transmits through abutment joints, with aperture and drainage producing pressure distributions different from a simple interpolation of reservoir level. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b233-v15-18","title":"裂隙水壓分布：定量估算","titleEn":"Joint water-pressure distribution: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b233-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「裂隙水壓分布」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Joint water-pressure distribution” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設矩形節理面200 m²，壓力由上緣0線性增到底部0.4 MPa，水壓合力40 MN，作用點距低壓邊2/3長度；限線性分布。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume joint area 200 m² with pressure rising linearly from zero to 0.4 MPa. Resultant is 40 MN at two-thirds length from the low-pressure edge, for a linear distribution. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：沿裂隙不同高程安裝代表性孔壓量測，核對與庫位變化的幅值和遲滯；將出水量與水壓分別報告，並積分非線性實測曲線比較教學三角形。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure representative pressures at several joint elevations and compare amplitude and lag with reservoir levels.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b233-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設矩形節理面200 m²，壓力由上緣0線性增到底部0.4 MPa，水壓合力40 MN，作用點距低壓邊2/3長度；限線性分布。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume joint area 200 m² with pressure rising linearly from zero to 0.4 MPa. Resultant is 40 MN at two-thirds length from the low-pressure edge, for a linear distribution.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b233-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「裂隙水壓分布」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Joint water-pressure distribution\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設矩形節理面200 m²，壓力由上緣0線性增到底部0.4 MPa，水壓合力40 MN，作用點距低壓邊2/3長度；限線性分布。","壩頂位移收斂就能證明所有局部最大應力都已收斂。","只要重新擬合後殘差變小，就證明原先結構異常已消失。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume joint area 200 m² with pressure rising linearly from zero to 0.4 MPa.","Converged crest displacement proves convergence of every local maximum stress.","A smaller residual after refitting proves the original structural anomaly has disappeared."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設矩形節理面200 m²，壓力由上緣0線性增到底部0.4 MPa，水壓合力40 MN，作用點距低壓邊2/3長度；限線性分布。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume joint area 200 m² with pressure rising linearly from zero to 0.4 MPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b233-v15-19","title":"裂隙水壓分布：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Joint water-pressure distribution: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b233-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「裂隙水壓分布」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Joint water-pressure distribution” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"沿裂隙不同高程安裝代表性孔壓量測，核對與庫位變化的幅值和遲滯；將出水量與水壓分別報告，並積分非線性實測曲線比較教學三角形。利用壓力積分求作用點以核對不利轉動力矩。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure representative pressures at several joint elevations and compare amplitude and lag with reservoir levels. Report discharge and pressure separately, integrating measured nonlinear profiles against the triangular teaching approximation. Locate the integrated pressure resultant to check its adverse rotational moment. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以裂隙水壓分布編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。沿裂隙不同高程安裝代表性孔壓量測，核對與庫位變化的幅值和遲滯；將出水量與水壓分別報告，並積分非線性實測曲線比較教學三角形。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for joint water-pressure distribution, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Measure representative pressures at several joint elevations and compare amplitude and lag with reservoir levels. Report discharge and pressure separately, integrating measured nonlinear profiles against the triangular teaching approximation.","failure":"注意干擾：出水量小可能因通道堵塞而水壓更高，不等於岸坡變乾。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Low discharge can indicate blockage with higher pressure rather than drier rock. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b233-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"沿裂隙不同高程安裝代表性孔壓量測，核對與庫位變化的幅值和遲滯；將出水量與水壓分別報告，並積分非線性實測曲線比較教學三角形。利用壓力積分求作用點以核對不利轉動力矩。","textEn":"Measure representative pressures at several joint elevations and compare amplitude and lag with reservoir levels. Report discharge and pressure separately, integrating measured nonlinear profiles against the triangular teaching approximation. Locate the integrated pressure resultant to check its adverse rotational moment.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b233-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以裂隙水壓分布編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。沿裂隙不同高程安裝代表性孔壓量測，核對與庫位變化的幅值和遲滯；將出水量與水壓分別報告，並積分非線性實測曲線比較教學三角形。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for joint water-pressure distribution, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Measure representative pressures at several joint elevations and compare amplitude and lag with reservoir levels. Report discharge and pressure separately, integrating measured nonlinear profiles against the triangular teaching approximation.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「裂隙水壓分布」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Joint water-pressure distribution\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","沿裂隙不同高程安裝代表性孔壓量測，核對與庫位變化的幅值和遲滯；將出水量與水壓分別報告，並積分非線性實測曲線比較教學三角形。","拱和懸臂的荷載比例可以任意指定而不影響位移相容。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Measure representative pressures at several joint elevations and compare amplitude and lag with reservoir levels.","Arch and cantilever shares can be chosen arbitrarily without affecting displacement compatibility."],"answer":1,"explanation":"沿裂隙不同高程安裝代表性孔壓量測，核對與庫位變化的幅值和遲滯；將出水量與水壓分別報告，並積分非線性實測曲線比較教學三角形。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure representative pressures at several joint elevations and compare amplitude and lag with reservoir levels. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b233-v15-20","title":"裂隙水壓分布：失效診斷","titleEn":"Joint water-pressure distribution: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b233-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「裂隙水壓分布」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Joint water-pressure distribution” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"出水量小可能因通道堵塞而水壓更高，不等於岸坡變乾。只用一個低壓測點代表整個滑面，會低估未排水區的合力和不利力矩。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Low discharge can indicate blockage with higher pressure rather than drier rock. Extending one low-pressure point over the full slip plane understates force and adverse moment in undrained portions. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：只用一個低壓測點代表整個滑面，會低估未排水區的合力和不利力矩。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Extending one low-pressure point over the full slip plane understates force and adverse moment in undrained portions.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「裂隙出水很少就能證明整個岸坡節理水壓很低。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Small joint discharge proves low water pressure throughout all abutment discontinuities.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b233-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"出水量小可能因通道堵塞而水壓更高，不等於岸坡變乾。只用一個低壓測點代表整個滑面，會低估未排水區的合力和不利力矩。","textEn":"Low discharge can indicate blockage with higher pressure rather than drier rock. Extending one low-pressure point over the full slip plane understates force and adverse moment in undrained portions.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b233-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「裂隙水壓分布」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Joint water-pressure distribution\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","完整岩芯彈性模數可以無條件等同整個節理岩體模數。","出水量小可能因通道堵塞而水壓更高，不等於岸坡變乾。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Intact-core elastic modulus can unconditionally represent the entire jointed rock mass.","Low discharge can indicate blockage with higher pressure rather than drier rock."],"answer":2,"explanation":"出水量小可能因通道堵塞而水壓更高，不等於岸坡變乾。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Low discharge can indicate blockage with higher pressure rather than drier rock. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b233-v15-21","title":"岩體柔度與拱座位移：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Rock compliance and abutment movement: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b233-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「岩體柔度與拱座位移」如何影響雙曲拱壩拱座分析的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Rock compliance and abutment movement” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Abutment analysis for double-curvature arch dams”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"岸坡會在推力下變形，拱座向外移動可能改變拱壩內力分配。岩體等效模數受節理和尺度影響，不能直接使用完整岩芯模數代替現地反應。 假設簡化壓縮區長20 m、面積400 m²、岩體E=10 GPa、推力40 MN，δ=FL/EA=0.2 mm；均質單軸類比，非岸坡真實三維解。 把基礎截斷面固定得太近會人工增硬，可能得到過小位移和錯誤應力。若只靠調整岩體模數配合壩頂量測，其他邊界錯誤可能被隱藏。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「岩體柔度與拱座位移」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Abutments deform under thrust and outward movement changes arch force distribution. Jointing and scale affect rock-mass modulus, preventing direct substitution of intact-core modulus for field response. Assume compressed zone length 20 m, area 400 m², rock-mass E=10 GPa and force 40 MN. δ=FL/EA=0.2 mm, a uniform uniaxial analogy rather than a real three-dimensional solution. Fixing foundation boundaries too close artificially stiffens the model and produces small displacements with wrong stresses. Adjusting modulus solely to fit crest movement can hide errors in other boundary assumptions. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Rock compliance and abutment movement” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設簡化壓縮區長20 m、面積400 m²、岩體E=10 GPa、推力40 MN，δ=FL/EA=0.2 mm；均質單軸類比，非岸坡真實三維解。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume compressed zone length 20 m, area 400 m², rock-mass E=10 GPa and force 40 MN. δ=FL/EA=0.2 mm, a uniform uniaxial analogy rather than a real three-dimensional solution.","failure":"常見誤解：「完整岩芯彈性模數可以無條件等同整個節理岩體模數。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Intact-core elastic modulus can unconditionally represent the entire jointed rock mass.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「岩體柔度與拱座位移」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Rock compliance and abutment movement”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b233-v15-21-k1","title":"岩體柔度與拱座位移","titleEn":"Rock compliance and abutment movement","text":"岸坡會在推力下變形，拱座向外移動可能改變拱壩內力分配。岩體等效模數受節理和尺度影響，不能直接使用完整岩芯模數代替現地反應。","textEn":"Abutments deform under thrust and outward movement changes arch force distribution. Jointing and scale affect rock-mass modulus, preventing direct substitution of intact-core modulus for field response.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b233-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：完整岩芯彈性模數可以無條件等同整個節理岩體模數。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Intact-core elastic modulus can unconditionally represent the entire jointed rock mass. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「岩體柔度與拱座位移」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Rock compliance and abutment movement\" is correct?","options":["岸坡會在推力下變形，拱座向外移動可能改變拱壩內力分配。","完整岩芯彈性模數可以無條件等同整個節理岩體模數。","接縫灌漿溫度只影響施工方便，不影響後續拱壩受力。"],"optionsEn":["Abutments deform under thrust and outward movement changes arch force distribution.","Intact-core elastic modulus can unconditionally represent the entire jointed rock mass.","Joint-grouting temperature affects convenience only and not later arch-dam structural behavior."],"answer":0,"explanation":"岸坡會在推力下變形，拱座向外移動可能改變拱壩內力分配。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Abutments deform under thrust and outward movement changes arch force distribution. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b233-v15-22","title":"岩體柔度與拱座位移：定量估算","titleEn":"Rock compliance and abutment movement: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b233-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「岩體柔度與拱座位移」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Rock compliance and abutment movement” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設簡化壓縮區長20 m、面積400 m²、岩體E=10 GPa、推力40 MN，δ=FL/EA=0.2 mm；均質單軸類比，非岸坡真實三維解。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume compressed zone length 20 m, area 400 m², rock-mass E=10 GPa and force 40 MN. δ=FL/EA=0.2 mm, a uniform uniaxial analogy rather than a real three-dimensional solution. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較現地變形試驗、節理調查與監測位移，建立模數範圍而非單值；改變基礎模型邊界距離和剛度，檢查壩體內力及拱座反力是否穩定。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare field deformation tests, joint mapping and monitored movements to establish a modulus range.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b233-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設簡化壓縮區長20 m、面積400 m²、岩體E=10 GPa、推力40 MN，δ=FL/EA=0.2 mm；均質單軸類比，非岸坡真實三維解。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume compressed zone length 20 m, area 400 m², rock-mass E=10 GPa and force 40 MN. δ=FL/EA=0.2 mm, a uniform uniaxial analogy rather than a real three-dimensional solution.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b233-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「岩體柔度與拱座位移」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Rock compliance and abutment movement\", which statement holds?","options":["把峰值地面加速度乘壩重就能完整代表三維地震反應。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設簡化壓縮區長20 m、面積400 m²、岩體E=10 GPa、推力40 MN，δ=FL/EA=0.2 mm。","薄拱平均壓應力足夠低就證明整座雙曲拱壩沒有拉應力。"],"optionsEn":["Peak ground acceleration times dam weight completely represents three-dimensional earthquake response.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume compressed zone length 20 m, area 400 m², rock-mass E=10 GPa and force 40 MN. δ=FL/EA=0.2 mm, a uniform uniaxial analogy rather than a real three-dimensional solution.","Low mean thin-arch compression proves there is no tensile stress anywhere in the dam."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設簡化壓縮區長20 m、面積400 m²、岩體E=10 GPa、推力40 MN，δ=FL/EA=0.2 mm；均質單軸類比，非岸坡真實三維解。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume compressed zone length 20 m, area 400 m², rock-mass E=10 GPa and force 40 MN. δ=FL/EA=0.2 mm, a uniform uniaxial analogy rather than a real three-dimensional solution. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b233-v15-23","title":"岩體柔度與拱座位移：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Rock compliance and abutment movement: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b233-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「岩體柔度與拱座位移」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Rock compliance and abutment movement” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較現地變形試驗、節理調查與監測位移，建立模數範圍而非單值；改變基礎模型邊界距離和剛度，檢查壩體內力及拱座反力是否穩定。將完整岩芯與岩體模數的來源分開標示。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare field deformation tests, joint mapping and monitored movements to establish a modulus range. Vary foundation boundary distance and stiffness and check stability of dam forces and abutment reactions. Identify intact-core and rock-mass modulus evidence as separate information sources. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以岩體柔度與拱座位移編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。比較現地變形試驗、節理調查與監測位移，建立模數範圍而非單值；改變基礎模型邊界距離和剛度，檢查壩體內力及拱座反力是否穩定。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for rock compliance and abutment movement, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Compare field deformation tests, joint mapping and monitored movements to establish a modulus range. Vary foundation boundary distance and stiffness and check stability of dam forces and abutment reactions.","failure":"注意干擾：把基礎截斷面固定得太近會人工增硬，可能得到過小位移和錯誤應力。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Fixing foundation boundaries too close artificially stiffens the model and produces small displacements with wrong stresses. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b233-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較現地變形試驗、節理調查與監測位移，建立模數範圍而非單值；改變基礎模型邊界距離和剛度，檢查壩體內力及拱座反力是否穩定。將完整岩芯與岩體模數的來源分開標示。","textEn":"Compare field deformation tests, joint mapping and monitored movements to establish a modulus range. Vary foundation boundary distance and stiffness and check stability of dam forces and abutment reactions. Identify intact-core and rock-mass modulus evidence as separate information sources.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b233-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以岩體柔度與拱座位移編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。比較現地變形試驗、節理調查與監測位移，建立模數範圍而非單值；改變基礎模型邊界距離和剛度，檢查壩體內力及拱座反力是否穩定。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for rock compliance and abutment movement, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Compare field deformation tests, joint mapping and monitored movements to establish a modulus range. Vary foundation boundary distance and stiffness and check stability of dam forces and abutment reactions.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「岩體柔度與拱座位移」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Rock compliance and abutment movement\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","岸坡承受的總推力越大就必定越穩定，方向不重要。","比較現地變形試驗、節理調查與監測位移，建立模數範圍而非單值；改變基礎模型邊界距離和剛度，檢查壩體內力及拱座反力是否穩定。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Greater total abutment thrust always improves stability regardless of its direction.","Compare field deformation tests, joint mapping and monitored movements to establish a modulus range."],"answer":2,"explanation":"比較現地變形試驗、節理調查與監測位移，建立模數範圍而非單值；改變基礎模型邊界距離和剛度，檢查壩體內力及拱座反力是否穩定。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare field deformation tests, joint mapping and monitored movements to establish a modulus range. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b233-v15-24","title":"岩體柔度與拱座位移：失效診斷","titleEn":"Rock compliance and abutment movement: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b233-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「岩體柔度與拱座位移」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Rock compliance and abutment movement” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把基礎截斷面固定得太近會人工增硬，可能得到過小位移和錯誤應力。若只靠調整岩體模數配合壩頂量測，其他邊界錯誤可能被隱藏。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Fixing foundation boundaries too close artificially stiffens the model and produces small displacements with wrong stresses. Adjusting modulus solely to fit crest movement can hide errors in other boundary assumptions. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：若只靠調整岩體模數配合壩頂量測，其他邊界錯誤可能被隱藏。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Adjusting modulus solely to fit crest movement can hide errors in other boundary assumptions.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「完整岩芯彈性模數可以無條件等同整個節理岩體模數。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Intact-core elastic modulus can unconditionally represent the entire jointed rock mass.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b233-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把基礎截斷面固定得太近會人工增硬，可能得到過小位移和錯誤應力。若只靠調整岩體模數配合壩頂量測，其他邊界錯誤可能被隱藏。","textEn":"Fixing foundation boundaries too close artificially stiffens the model and produces small displacements with wrong stresses. Adjusting modulus solely to fit crest movement can hide errors in other boundary assumptions.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b233-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「岩體柔度與拱座位移」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Rock compliance and abutment movement\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把基礎截斷面固定得太近會人工增硬，可能得到過小位移和錯誤應力。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","接縫灌漿溫度只影響施工方便，不影響後續拱壩受力。"],"optionsEn":["Fixing foundation boundaries too close artificially stiffens the model and produces small displacements with wrong stresses.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Joint-grouting temperature affects convenience only and not later arch-dam structural behavior."],"answer":0,"explanation":"把基礎截斷面固定得太近會人工增硬，可能得到過小位移和錯誤應力。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Fixing foundation boundaries too close artificially stiffens the model and produces small displacements with wrong stresses. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b233-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「封拱溫度與接縫閉合」與「網格收斂與局部奇異」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Closure temperature and joint closure\" and \"Mesh convergence and singularity\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b233-v15-25","title":"封拱溫度與接縫閉合：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Closure temperature and joint closure: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b233-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「封拱溫度與接縫閉合」如何影響雙曲拱壩拱座分析的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Closure temperature and joint closure” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Abutment analysis for double-curvature arch dams”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"拱壩接縫灌漿後形成不同於分離懸臂的整體作用，封拱溫度決定後續升溫壓縮和降溫張開傾向。溫度是結構初始狀態的一部分。 假設有效拱長200 m、α=10⁻⁵/K、相對封拱溫度下降8 K，自由縮短16 mm；真實拘束會轉成接縫位移和應力，非直接開縫總量。 把所有壩段視為同時同溫度閉合會忽略施工分期，局部灌漿不完整也可能保留柔弱面。若模型沒有記錄封拱狀態，溫度應力的符號可能被錯判。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「封拱溫度與接縫閉合」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Joint grouting creates an integrated arch distinct from separate cantilevers. Closure temperature establishes later warming compression and cooling-opening tendencies, making temperature part of the structural initial state. Assume effective arch length 200 m, α=10⁻⁵/K and cooling eight kelvin below closure temperature. Free shortening is 16 mm; actual restraint converts it into movement and stress rather than this exact total opening. Assuming simultaneous equal-temperature closure misses construction staging, and incomplete grouting leaves compliant interfaces. Without the closure state, even the sign of inferred thermal stress can be misinterpreted. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Closure temperature and joint closure” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設有效拱長200 m、α=10⁻⁵/K、相對封拱溫度下降8 K，自由縮短16 mm；真實拘束會轉成接縫位移和應力，非直接開縫總量。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume effective arch length 200 m, α=10⁻⁵/K and cooling eight kelvin below closure temperature.","failure":"常見誤解：「接縫灌漿溫度只影響施工方便，不影響後續拱壩受力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Joint-grouting temperature affects convenience only and not later arch-dam structural behavior.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「封拱溫度與接縫閉合」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Closure temperature and joint closure”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b233-v15-25-k1","title":"封拱溫度與接縫閉合","titleEn":"Closure temperature and joint closure","text":"拱壩接縫灌漿後形成不同於分離懸臂的整體作用，封拱溫度決定後續升溫壓縮和降溫張開傾向。溫度是結構初始狀態的一部分。","textEn":"Joint grouting creates an integrated arch distinct from separate cantilevers. Closure temperature establishes later warming compression and cooling-opening tendencies, making temperature part of the structural initial state.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b233-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：接縫灌漿溫度只影響施工方便，不影響後續拱壩受力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Joint-grouting temperature affects convenience only and not later arch-dam structural behavior. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「封拱溫度與接縫閉合」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Closure temperature and joint closure\" is correct?","options":["接縫灌漿溫度只影響施工方便，不影響後續拱壩受力。","拱壩接縫灌漿後形成不同於分離懸臂的整體作用，封拱溫度決定後續升溫壓縮和降溫張開傾向。","壩頂位移收斂就能證明所有局部最大應力都已收斂。"],"optionsEn":["Joint-grouting temperature affects convenience only and not later arch-dam structural behavior.","Joint grouting creates an integrated arch distinct from separate cantilevers.","Converged crest displacement proves convergence of every local maximum stress."],"answer":1,"explanation":"拱壩接縫灌漿後形成不同於分離懸臂的整體作用，封拱溫度決定後續升溫壓縮和降溫張開傾向。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Joint grouting creates an integrated arch distinct from separate cantilevers. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b233-v15-26","title":"封拱溫度與接縫閉合：定量估算","titleEn":"Closure temperature and joint closure: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b233-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「封拱溫度與接縫閉合」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Closure temperature and joint closure” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設有效拱長200 m、α=10⁻⁵/K、相對封拱溫度下降8 K，自由縮短16 mm；真實拘束會轉成接縫位移和應力，非直接開縫總量。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume effective arch length 200 m, α=10⁻⁵/K and cooling eight kelvin below closure temperature. Free shortening is 16 mm; actual restraint converts it into movement and stress rather than this exact total opening. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對灌漿時的多點溫度而非單一氣溫，將接縫計零點與施工日期連結；比較後續同庫位不同溫度的變形，確認模型初始狀態可重現觀測。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check multi-point grouting temperatures rather than ambient air alone and link joint-meter zeros to construction dates.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b233-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設有效拱長200 m、α=10⁻⁵/K、相對封拱溫度下降8 K，自由縮短16 mm；真實拘束會轉成接縫位移和應力，非直接開縫總量。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume effective arch length 200 m, α=10⁻⁵/K and cooling eight kelvin below closure temperature. Free shortening is 16 mm; actual restraint converts it into movement and stress rather than this exact total opening.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b233-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「封拱溫度與接縫閉合」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Closure temperature and joint closure\", which statement holds?","options":["只要重新擬合後殘差變小，就證明原先結構異常已消失。","拱和懸臂的荷載比例可以任意指定而不影響位移相容。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設有效拱長200 m、α=10⁻⁵/K、相對封拱溫度下降8 K，自由縮短16 mm。"],"optionsEn":["A smaller residual after refitting proves the original structural anomaly has disappeared.","Arch and cantilever shares can be chosen arbitrarily without affecting displacement compatibility.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume effective arch length 200 m, α=10⁻⁵/K and cooling eight kelvin below closure temperature."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設有效拱長200 m、α=10⁻⁵/K、相對封拱溫度下降8 K，自由縮短16 mm；真實拘束會轉成接縫位移和應力，非直接開縫總量。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume effective arch length 200 m, α=10⁻⁵/K and cooling eight kelvin below closure temperature. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b233-v15-27","title":"封拱溫度與接縫閉合：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Closure temperature and joint closure: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b233-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「封拱溫度與接縫閉合」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Closure temperature and joint closure” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對灌漿時的多點溫度而非單一氣溫，將接縫計零點與施工日期連結；比較後續同庫位不同溫度的變形，確認模型初始狀態可重現觀測。對各灌漿區塊保留自己的封拱溫度紀錄。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check multi-point grouting temperatures rather than ambient air alone and link joint-meter zeros to construction dates. Compare deformation at equal reservoir level but different temperature to test the initial-state model. Retain a separate closure-temperature record for every grouted block group. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以封拱溫度與接縫閉合編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。核對灌漿時的多點溫度而非單一氣溫，將接縫計零點與施工日期連結；比較後續同庫位不同溫度的變形，確認模型初始狀態可重現觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for closure temperature and joint closure, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Check multi-point grouting temperatures rather than ambient air alone and link joint-meter zeros to construction dates. Compare deformation at equal reservoir level but different temperature to test the initial-state model.","failure":"注意干擾：把所有壩段視為同時同溫度閉合會忽略施工分期，局部灌漿不完整也可能保留柔弱面。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Assuming simultaneous equal-temperature closure misses construction staging, and incomplete grouting leaves compliant interfaces. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b233-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對灌漿時的多點溫度而非單一氣溫，將接縫計零點與施工日期連結；比較後續同庫位不同溫度的變形，確認模型初始狀態可重現觀測。對各灌漿區塊保留自己的封拱溫度紀錄。","textEn":"Check multi-point grouting temperatures rather than ambient air alone and link joint-meter zeros to construction dates. Compare deformation at equal reservoir level but different temperature to test the initial-state model. Retain a separate closure-temperature record for every grouted block group.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b233-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以封拱溫度與接縫閉合編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。核對灌漿時的多點溫度而非單一氣溫，將接縫計零點與施工日期連結；比較後續同庫位不同溫度的變形，確認模型初始狀態可重現觀測。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for closure temperature and joint closure, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Check multi-point grouting temperatures rather than ambient air alone and link joint-meter zeros to construction dates. Compare deformation at equal reservoir level but different temperature to test the initial-state model.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「封拱溫度與接縫閉合」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Closure temperature and joint closure\"?","options":["核對灌漿時的多點溫度而非單一氣溫，將接縫計零點與施工日期連結；比較後續同庫位不同溫度的變形，確認模型初始狀態可重現觀測。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","岩石單軸強度很高就能排除沿節理滑動的岸坡失穩。"],"optionsEn":["Check multi-point grouting temperatures rather than ambient air alone and link joint-meter zeros to construction dates.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","High intact-rock compressive strength rules out abutment failure by joint sliding."],"answer":0,"explanation":"核對灌漿時的多點溫度而非單一氣溫，將接縫計零點與施工日期連結；比較後續同庫位不同溫度的變形，確認模型初始狀態可重現觀測。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check multi-point grouting temperatures rather than ambient air alone and link joint-meter zeros to construction dates. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b233-v15-28","title":"封拱溫度與接縫閉合：失效診斷","titleEn":"Closure temperature and joint closure: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b233-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「封拱溫度與接縫閉合」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Closure temperature and joint closure” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把所有壩段視為同時同溫度閉合會忽略施工分期，局部灌漿不完整也可能保留柔弱面。若模型沒有記錄封拱狀態，溫度應力的符號可能被錯判。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Assuming simultaneous equal-temperature closure misses construction staging, and incomplete grouting leaves compliant interfaces. Without the closure state, even the sign of inferred thermal stress can be misinterpreted. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：若模型沒有記錄封拱狀態，溫度應力的符號可能被錯判。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Without the closure state, even the sign of inferred thermal stress can be misinterpreted.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「接縫灌漿溫度只影響施工方便，不影響後續拱壩受力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Joint-grouting temperature affects convenience only and not later arch-dam structural behavior.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b233-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把所有壩段視為同時同溫度閉合會忽略施工分期，局部灌漿不完整也可能保留柔弱面。若模型沒有記錄封拱狀態，溫度應力的符號可能被錯判。","textEn":"Assuming simultaneous equal-temperature closure misses construction staging, and incomplete grouting leaves compliant interfaces. Without the closure state, even the sign of inferred thermal stress can be misinterpreted.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b233-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「封拱溫度與接縫閉合」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Closure temperature and joint closure\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","把所有壩段視為同時同溫度閉合會忽略施工分期，局部灌漿不完整也可能保留柔弱面。","壩頂位移收斂就能證明所有局部最大應力都已收斂。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Assuming simultaneous equal-temperature closure misses construction staging, and incomplete grouting leaves compliant interfaces.","Converged crest displacement proves convergence of every local maximum stress."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把所有壩段視為同時同溫度閉合會忽略施工分期，局部灌漿不完整也可能保留柔弱面。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Assuming simultaneous equal-temperature closure misses construction staging, and incomplete grouting leaves compliant interfaces. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b233-v15-29","title":"網格收斂與局部奇異：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Mesh convergence and singularity: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b233-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「網格收斂與局部奇異」如何影響雙曲拱壩拱座分析的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Mesh convergence and singularity” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Abutment analysis for double-curvature arch dams”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"三維分析須區分真正的應力集中和幾何尖角造成的數值奇異。網格愈細不一定讓尖角最大應力收斂，應同時檢查位移、能量與有限區域平均。 假設兩次細化壩頂位移由12.0降至11.7 mm，相對差0.3/11.7=2.564%；此差只衡量該位移，不能保證局部應力已收斂。 只報最細網格最大應力可能讓數值奇異冒充材料失效，反之只看位移收斂也會漏掉接觸邊緣問題。收斂是特定輸出量的性質，不能概括全部結果。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「網格收斂與局部奇異」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Three-dimensional analysis must distinguish physical concentration from numerical singularities at sharp corners. Finer meshes may not converge the point maximum, requiring displacement, energy and finite-area averages to be checked together. Assume refined crest displacement changes from 12.0 to 11.7 mm. Relative difference is 2.564 percent, describing this displacement only rather than proving local stress convergence. Reporting only the finest-mesh maximum can mistake a singularity for material failure, while displacement convergence can miss contact-edge issues. Convergence applies to a specific output and cannot certify every model result. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Mesh convergence and singularity” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設兩次細化壩頂位移由12.0降至11.7 mm，相對差0.3/11.7=2.564%；此差只衡量該位移，不能保證局部應力已收斂。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume refined crest displacement changes from 12.0 to 11.7 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「壩頂位移收斂就能證明所有局部最大應力都已收斂。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Converged crest displacement proves convergence of every local maximum stress.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「網格收斂與局部奇異」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Mesh convergence and singularity”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b233-v15-29-k1","title":"網格收斂與局部奇異","titleEn":"Mesh convergence and singularity","text":"三維分析須區分真正的應力集中和幾何尖角造成的數值奇異。網格愈細不一定讓尖角最大應力收斂，應同時檢查位移、能量與有限區域平均。","textEn":"Three-dimensional analysis must distinguish physical concentration from numerical singularities at sharp corners. Finer meshes may not converge the point maximum, requiring displacement, energy and finite-area averages to be checked together.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b233-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：壩頂位移收斂就能證明所有局部最大應力都已收斂。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Converged crest displacement proves convergence of every local maximum stress. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「網格收斂與局部奇異」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Mesh convergence and singularity\" is correct?","options":["壩頂位移收斂就能證明所有局部最大應力都已收斂。","把峰值地面加速度乘壩重就能完整代表三維地震反應。","三維分析須區分真正的應力集中和幾何尖角造成的數值奇異。"],"optionsEn":["Converged crest displacement proves convergence of every local maximum stress.","Peak ground acceleration times dam weight completely represents three-dimensional earthquake response.","Three-dimensional analysis must distinguish physical concentration from numerical singularities at sharp corners."],"answer":2,"explanation":"三維分析須區分真正的應力集中和幾何尖角造成的數值奇異。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Three-dimensional analysis must distinguish physical concentration from numerical singularities at sharp corners. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b233-v15-30","title":"網格收斂與局部奇異：定量估算","titleEn":"Mesh convergence and singularity: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b233-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「網格收斂與局部奇異」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Mesh convergence and singularity” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設兩次細化壩頂位移由12.0降至11.7 mm，相對差0.3/11.7=2.564%；此差只衡量該位移，不能保證局部應力已收斂。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume refined crest displacement changes from 12.0 to 11.7 mm. Relative difference is 2.564 percent, describing this displacement only rather than proving local stress convergence. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：保持材料與荷載不變細化網格，分別追蹤位移、反力和局部平均應力；檢查尖角最大值是否隨單元尺寸無界增加，並以合理幾何圓角測試模型敏感性。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Refine meshes with unchanged materials and loads, tracking displacement, reactions and local average stress separately.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b233-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設兩次細化壩頂位移由12.0降至11.7 mm，相對差0.3/11.7=2.564%；此差只衡量該位移，不能保證局部應力已收斂。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume refined crest displacement changes from 12.0 to 11.7 mm. Relative difference is 2.564 percent, describing this displacement only rather than proving local stress convergence.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b233-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「網格收斂與局部奇異」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Mesh convergence and singularity\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設兩次細化壩頂位移由12.0降至11.7 mm，相對差0.3/11.7=2.564%。","薄拱平均壓應力足夠低就證明整座雙曲拱壩沒有拉應力。","岸坡承受的總推力越大就必定越穩定，方向不重要。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume refined crest displacement changes from 12.0 to 11.7 mm.","Low mean thin-arch compression proves there is no tensile stress anywhere in the dam.","Greater total abutment thrust always improves stability regardless of its direction."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設兩次細化壩頂位移由12.0降至11.7 mm，相對差0.3/11.7=2.564%；此差只衡量該位移，不能保證局部應力已收斂。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume refined crest displacement changes from 12.0 to 11.7 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b233-v15-31","title":"網格收斂與局部奇異：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Mesh convergence and singularity: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b233-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「網格收斂與局部奇異」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Mesh convergence and singularity” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"保持材料與荷載不變細化網格，分別追蹤位移、反力和局部平均應力；檢查尖角最大值是否隨單元尺寸無界增加，並以合理幾何圓角測試模型敏感性。對有限面積平均應力另做網格收斂曲線。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Refine meshes with unchanged materials and loads, tracking displacement, reactions and local average stress separately. Check whether corner maxima grow without bound and test sensitivity to physically reasonable geometric rounding. Construct a separate mesh-convergence curve for stress averaged over finite areas. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以網格收斂與局部奇異編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。保持材料與荷載不變細化網格，分別追蹤位移、反力和局部平均應力；檢查尖角最大值是否隨單元尺寸無界增加，並以合理幾何圓角測試模型敏感性。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for mesh convergence and singularity, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Refine meshes with unchanged materials and loads, tracking displacement, reactions and local average stress separately. Check whether corner maxima grow without bound and test sensitivity to physically reasonable geometric rounding.","failure":"注意干擾：只報最細網格最大應力可能讓數值奇異冒充材料失效，反之只看位移收斂也會漏掉接觸邊緣問題。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Reporting only the finest-mesh maximum can mistake a singularity for material failure, while displacement convergence can miss contact-edge issues. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b233-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"保持材料與荷載不變細化網格，分別追蹤位移、反力和局部平均應力；檢查尖角最大值是否隨單元尺寸無界增加，並以合理幾何圓角測試模型敏感性。對有限面積平均應力另做網格收斂曲線。","textEn":"Refine meshes with unchanged materials and loads, tracking displacement, reactions and local average stress separately. Check whether corner maxima grow without bound and test sensitivity to physically reasonable geometric rounding. Construct a separate mesh-convergence curve for stress averaged over finite areas.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b233-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以網格收斂與局部奇異編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。保持材料與荷載不變細化網格，分別追蹤位移、反力和局部平均應力；檢查尖角最大值是否隨單元尺寸無界增加，並以合理幾何圓角測試模型敏感性。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for mesh convergence and singularity, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Refine meshes with unchanged materials and loads, tracking displacement, reactions and local average stress separately. Check whether corner maxima grow without bound and test sensitivity to physically reasonable geometric rounding.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「網格收斂與局部奇異」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Mesh convergence and singularity\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","保持材料與荷載不變細化網格，分別追蹤位移、反力和局部平均應力；檢查尖角最大值是否隨單元尺寸無界增加，並以合理幾何圓角測試模型敏感性。","裂隙出水很少就能證明整個岸坡節理水壓很低。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Refine meshes with unchanged materials and loads, tracking displacement, reactions and local average stress separately.","Small joint discharge proves low water pressure throughout all abutment discontinuities."],"answer":1,"explanation":"保持材料與荷載不變細化網格，分別追蹤位移、反力和局部平均應力；檢查尖角最大值是否隨單元尺寸無界增加，並以合理幾何圓角測試模型敏感性。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Refine meshes with unchanged materials and loads, tracking displacement, reactions and local average stress separately. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b233-v15-32","title":"網格收斂與局部奇異：失效診斷","titleEn":"Mesh convergence and singularity: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b233-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「網格收斂與局部奇異」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Mesh convergence and singularity” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只報最細網格最大應力可能讓數值奇異冒充材料失效，反之只看位移收斂也會漏掉接觸邊緣問題。收斂是特定輸出量的性質，不能概括全部結果。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Reporting only the finest-mesh maximum can mistake a singularity for material failure, while displacement convergence can miss contact-edge issues. Convergence applies to a specific output and cannot certify every model result. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：收斂是特定輸出量的性質，不能概括全部結果。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Convergence applies to a specific output and cannot certify every model result.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「壩頂位移收斂就能證明所有局部最大應力都已收斂。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Converged crest displacement proves convergence of every local maximum stress.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b233-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只報最細網格最大應力可能讓數值奇異冒充材料失效，反之只看位移收斂也會漏掉接觸邊緣問題。收斂是特定輸出量的性質，不能概括全部結果。","textEn":"Reporting only the finest-mesh maximum can mistake a singularity for material failure, while displacement convergence can miss contact-edge issues. Convergence applies to a specific output and cannot certify every model result.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b233-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「網格收斂與局部奇異」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Mesh convergence and singularity\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","把峰值地面加速度乘壩重就能完整代表三維地震反應。","只報最細網格最大應力可能讓數值奇異冒充材料失效，反之只看位移收斂也會漏掉接觸邊緣問題。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Peak ground acceleration times dam weight completely represents three-dimensional earthquake response.","Reporting only the finest-mesh maximum can mistake a singularity for material failure, while displacement convergence can miss contact-edge issues."],"answer":2,"explanation":"只報最細網格最大應力可能讓數值奇異冒充材料失效，反之只看位移收斂也會漏掉接觸邊緣問題。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Reporting only the finest-mesh maximum can mistake a singularity for material failure, while displacement convergence can miss contact-edge issues. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b233-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「地震慣性與附加水質量」與「水溫荷載與監測殘差」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Seismic inertia and added water mass\" and \"Hydrothermal effects and monitoring residuals\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b233-v15-33","title":"地震慣性與附加水質量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Seismic inertia and added water mass: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b233-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「地震慣性與附加水質量」如何影響雙曲拱壩拱座分析的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Seismic inertia and added water mass” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Abutment analysis for double-curvature arch dams”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"地震作用同時包含壩體、基礎和庫水的動力互制，靜力慣性項只提供量級。附加水質量隨頻率與邊界改變，不能任意當成固定壩重增加。 取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設等效振動質量5 million kg、水平加速度0.1g，慣性力ma=4.905 MN；僅單模態量級，不含動力放大或真實庫水附加質量。 把峰值地面加速度直接乘全部壩重不能代表每點同相加速，基礎柔度與輻射阻尼也會改變反應。忽略水庫耦合可能錯估頻率和壩頂放大。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「地震慣性與附加水質量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Earthquake response involves dam, foundation and reservoir interaction. A static inertia term gives only a scale, while hydrodynamic added mass depends on frequency and boundaries rather than an arbitrary fixed weight increase. Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume equivalent vibrating mass 5 million kg and horizontal acceleration 0.1g. Inertia ma=4.905 MN, a single-mode scale without dynamic amplification or actual reservoir added mass. Peak ground acceleration times total weight does not mean every point accelerates in phase. Foundation compliance, radiation damping and reservoir coupling can change frequencies and crest amplification substantially. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Seismic inertia and added water mass” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s².","failure":"常見誤解：「把峰值地面加速度乘壩重就能完整代表三維地震反應。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Peak ground acceleration times dam weight completely represents three-dimensional earthquake response.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「地震慣性與附加水質量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Seismic inertia and added water mass”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b233-v15-33-k1","title":"地震慣性與附加水質量","titleEn":"Seismic inertia and added water mass","text":"地震作用同時包含壩體、基礎和庫水的動力互制，靜力慣性項只提供量級。附加水質量隨頻率與邊界改變，不能任意當成固定壩重增加。","textEn":"Earthquake response involves dam, foundation and reservoir interaction. A static inertia term gives only a scale, while hydrodynamic added mass depends on frequency and boundaries rather than an arbitrary fixed weight increase.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b233-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：把峰值地面加速度乘壩重就能完整代表三維地震反應。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Peak ground acceleration times dam weight completely represents three-dimensional earthquake response. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「地震慣性與附加水質量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Seismic inertia and added water mass\" is correct?","options":["地震作用同時包含壩體、基礎和庫水的動力互制，靜力慣性項只提供量級。","把峰值地面加速度乘壩重就能完整代表三維地震反應。","只要重新擬合後殘差變小，就證明原先結構異常已消失。"],"optionsEn":["Earthquake response involves dam, foundation and reservoir interaction.","Peak ground acceleration times dam weight completely represents three-dimensional earthquake response.","A smaller residual after refitting proves the original structural anomaly has disappeared."],"answer":0,"explanation":"地震作用同時包含壩體、基礎和庫水的動力互制，靜力慣性項只提供量級。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Earthquake response involves dam, foundation and reservoir interaction. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b233-v15-34","title":"地震慣性與附加水質量：定量估算","titleEn":"Seismic inertia and added water mass: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b233-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「地震慣性與附加水質量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Seismic inertia and added water mass” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設等效振動質量5 million kg、水平加速度0.1g，慣性力ma=4.905 MN；僅單模態量級，不含動力放大或真實庫水附加質量。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume equivalent vibrating mass 5 million kg and horizontal acceleration 0.1g. Inertia ma=4.905 MN, a single-mode scale without dynamic amplification or actual reservoir added mass. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以觀測或辨識的模態檢查頻率與阻尼，核對輸入地震在基礎和自由場的定義；比較含水與無水模型的反應，保留頻率相關邊界而非只調總質量。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check identified frequencies and damping and distinguish foundation input from free-field motion.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b233-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設等效振動質量5 million kg、水平加速度0.1g，慣性力ma=4.905 MN；僅單模態量級，不含動力放大或真實庫水附加質量。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume equivalent vibrating mass 5 million kg and horizontal acceleration 0.1g. Inertia ma=4.905 MN, a single-mode scale without dynamic amplification or actual reservoir added mass.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b233-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「地震慣性與附加水質量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Seismic inertia and added water mass\", which statement holds?","options":["拱和懸臂的荷載比例可以任意指定而不影響位移相容。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。","岩石單軸強度很高就能排除沿節理滑動的岸坡失穩。"],"optionsEn":["Arch and cantilever shares can be chosen arbitrarily without affecting displacement compatibility.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s².","High intact-rock compressive strength rules out abutment failure by joint sliding."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b233-v15-35","title":"地震慣性與附加水質量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Seismic inertia and added water mass: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b233-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「地震慣性與附加水質量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Seismic inertia and added water mass” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以觀測或辨識的模態檢查頻率與阻尼，核對輸入地震在基礎和自由場的定義；比較含水與無水模型的反應，保留頻率相關邊界而非只調總質量。以能量平衡檢查附加水質量模型的合理性。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check identified frequencies and damping and distinguish foundation input from free-field motion. Compare models with and without water, retaining frequency-dependent boundaries rather than adjusting total mass alone. Use an energy balance to check the plausibility of added-water-mass modeling. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以地震慣性與附加水質量編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。以觀測或辨識的模態檢查頻率與阻尼，核對輸入地震在基礎和自由場的定義；比較含水與無水模型的反應，保留頻率相關邊界而非只調總質量。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for seismic inertia and added water mass, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Check identified frequencies and damping and distinguish foundation input from free-field motion. Compare models with and without water, retaining frequency-dependent boundaries rather than adjusting total mass alone.","failure":"注意干擾：把峰值地面加速度直接乘全部壩重不能代表每點同相加速，基礎柔度與輻射阻尼也會改變反應。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Peak ground acceleration times total weight does not mean every point accelerates in phase. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b233-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以觀測或辨識的模態檢查頻率與阻尼，核對輸入地震在基礎和自由場的定義；比較含水與無水模型的反應，保留頻率相關邊界而非只調總質量。以能量平衡檢查附加水質量模型的合理性。","textEn":"Check identified frequencies and damping and distinguish foundation input from free-field motion. Compare models with and without water, retaining frequency-dependent boundaries rather than adjusting total mass alone. Use an energy balance to check the plausibility of added-water-mass modeling.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b233-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以地震慣性與附加水質量編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。以觀測或辨識的模態檢查頻率與阻尼，核對輸入地震在基礎和自由場的定義；比較含水與無水模型的反應，保留頻率相關邊界而非只調總質量。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for seismic inertia and added water mass, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Check identified frequencies and damping and distinguish foundation input from free-field motion. Compare models with and without water, retaining frequency-dependent boundaries rather than adjusting total mass alone.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「地震慣性與附加水質量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Seismic inertia and added water mass\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","完整岩芯彈性模數可以無條件等同整個節理岩體模數。","以觀測或辨識的模態檢查頻率與阻尼，核對輸入地震在基礎和自由場的定義；比較含水與無水模型的反應，保留頻率相關邊界而非只調總質量。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Intact-core elastic modulus can unconditionally represent the entire jointed rock mass.","Check identified frequencies and damping and distinguish foundation input from free-field motion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以觀測或辨識的模態檢查頻率與阻尼，核對輸入地震在基礎和自由場的定義；比較含水與無水模型的反應，保留頻率相關邊界而非只調總質量。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check identified frequencies and damping and distinguish foundation input from free-field motion. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b233-v15-36","title":"地震慣性與附加水質量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Seismic inertia and added water mass: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b233-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「地震慣性與附加水質量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Seismic inertia and added water mass” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把峰值地面加速度直接乘全部壩重不能代表每點同相加速，基礎柔度與輻射阻尼也會改變反應。忽略水庫耦合可能錯估頻率和壩頂放大。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Peak ground acceleration times total weight does not mean every point accelerates in phase. Foundation compliance, radiation damping and reservoir coupling can change frequencies and crest amplification substantially. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：忽略水庫耦合可能錯估頻率和壩頂放大。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Foundation compliance, radiation damping and reservoir coupling can change frequencies and crest amplification substantially.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「把峰值地面加速度乘壩重就能完整代表三維地震反應。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Peak ground acceleration times dam weight completely represents three-dimensional earthquake response.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b233-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把峰值地面加速度直接乘全部壩重不能代表每點同相加速，基礎柔度與輻射阻尼也會改變反應。忽略水庫耦合可能錯估頻率和壩頂放大。","textEn":"Peak ground acceleration times total weight does not mean every point accelerates in phase. Foundation compliance, radiation damping and reservoir coupling can change frequencies and crest amplification substantially.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b233-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「地震慣性與附加水質量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Seismic inertia and added water mass\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把峰值地面加速度直接乘全部壩重不能代表每點同相加速，基礎柔度與輻射阻尼也會改變反應。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","只要重新擬合後殘差變小，就證明原先結構異常已消失。"],"optionsEn":["Peak ground acceleration times total weight does not mean every point accelerates in phase.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A smaller residual after refitting proves the original structural anomaly has disappeared."],"answer":0,"explanation":"把峰值地面加速度直接乘全部壩重不能代表每點同相加速，基礎柔度與輻射阻尼也會改變反應。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Peak ground acceleration times total weight does not mean every point accelerates in phase. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b233-v15-37","title":"水溫荷載與監測殘差：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Hydrothermal effects and monitoring residuals: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b233-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「水溫荷載與監測殘差」如何影響雙曲拱壩拱座分析的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Hydrothermal effects and monitoring residuals” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Abutment analysis for double-curvature arch dams”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"拱壩位移同時受庫水位、溫度和時間影響，異常診斷需先扣除可解釋的正常反應。統計模型只能在已驗證範圍內描述資料，不直接證明結構安全。 線性係數分別為0.1 mm/m與0.2 mm/K。假設教學位移模型d=0.1ΔH+0.2ΔT mm，ΔH=10 m、ΔT=5 K，預測2 mm；觀測2.6 mm則殘差0.6 mm，非警戒值。 高度相關的水位與溫度會讓係數難以識別，模型也可能把長期損傷吸收為時間趨勢。重新訓練前若未檢查原因，異常可能被數學上消除卻仍存在。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「水溫荷載與監測殘差」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Arch displacement responds to water level, temperature and time, so anomaly interpretation first removes explainable normal behavior. Statistical models describe validated data ranges rather than independently proving structural safety. The linear coefficients are 0.1 mm/m and 0.2 mm/K, respectively. Assume teaching displacement d=0.1ΔH+0.2ΔT mm with ΔH=10 m and ΔT=5 K. Prediction is 2 mm; observation 2.6 mm leaves residual 0.6 mm, not an alarm threshold. Correlated level and temperature make coefficients difficult to identify, and a time trend can absorb deterioration. Retraining without investigating causes may mathematically erase an anomaly while its physical source remains. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Hydrothermal effects and monitoring residuals” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：線性係數分別為0.1 mm/m與0.2 mm/K。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: The linear coefficients are 0.1 mm/m and 0.2 mm/K, respectively.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要重新擬合後殘差變小，就證明原先結構異常已消失。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A smaller residual after refitting proves the original structural anomaly has disappeared.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「水溫荷載與監測殘差」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Hydrothermal effects and monitoring residuals”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b233-v15-37-k1","title":"水溫荷載與監測殘差","titleEn":"Hydrothermal effects and monitoring residuals","text":"拱壩位移同時受庫水位、溫度和時間影響，異常診斷需先扣除可解釋的正常反應。統計模型只能在已驗證範圍內描述資料，不直接證明結構安全。","textEn":"Arch displacement responds to water level, temperature and time, so anomaly interpretation first removes explainable normal behavior. Statistical models describe validated data ranges rather than independently proving structural safety.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b233-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要重新擬合後殘差變小，就證明原先結構異常已消失。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A smaller residual after refitting proves the original structural anomaly has disappeared. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「水溫荷載與監測殘差」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Hydrothermal effects and monitoring residuals\" is correct?","options":["只要重新擬合後殘差變小，就證明原先結構異常已消失。","拱壩位移同時受庫水位、溫度和時間影響，異常診斷需先扣除可解釋的正常反應。","薄拱平均壓應力足夠低就證明整座雙曲拱壩沒有拉應力。"],"optionsEn":["A smaller residual after refitting proves the original structural anomaly has disappeared.","Arch displacement responds to water level, temperature and time, so anomaly interpretation first removes explainable normal behavior.","Low mean thin-arch compression proves there is no tensile stress anywhere in the dam."],"answer":1,"explanation":"拱壩位移同時受庫水位、溫度和時間影響，異常診斷需先扣除可解釋的正常反應。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Arch displacement responds to water level, temperature and time, so anomaly interpretation first removes explainable normal behavior. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b233-v15-38","title":"水溫荷載與監測殘差：定量估算","titleEn":"Hydrothermal effects and monitoring residuals: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b233-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「水溫荷載與監測殘差」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Hydrothermal effects and monitoring residuals” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：線性係數分別為0.1 mm/m與0.2 mm/K。假設教學位移模型d=0.1ΔH+0.2ΔT mm，ΔH=10 m、ΔT=5 K，預測2 mm；觀測2.6 mm則殘差0.6 mm，非警戒值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: The linear coefficients are 0.1 mm/m and 0.2 mm/K, respectively. Assume teaching displacement d=0.1ΔH+0.2ΔT mm with ΔH=10 m and ΔT=5 K. Prediction is 2 mm; observation 2.6 mm leaves residual 0.6 mm, not an alarm threshold. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用獨立時段驗證模型並檢查殘差隨季節和水位的結構，核對儀器更換與基準漂移；將局部裂縫、滲流與位移證據交叉比較，避免單靠統計超限下結論。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Validate on an independent period and examine residual patterns with season and level, checking instrument changes and datum drift.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b233-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：線性係數分別為0.1 mm/m與0.2 mm/K。假設教學位移模型d=0.1ΔH+0.2ΔT mm，ΔH=10 m、ΔT=5 K，預測2 mm；觀測2.6 mm則殘差0.6 mm，非警戒值。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: The linear coefficients are 0.1 mm/m and 0.2 mm/K, respectively. Assume teaching displacement d=0.1ΔH+0.2ΔT mm with ΔH=10 m and ΔT=5 K. Prediction is 2 mm; observation 2.6 mm leaves residual 0.6 mm, not an alarm threshold.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b233-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「水溫荷載與監測殘差」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Hydrothermal effects and monitoring residuals\", which statement holds?","options":["岸坡承受的總推力越大就必定越穩定，方向不重要。","裂隙出水很少就能證明整個岸坡節理水壓很低。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：線性係數分別為0.1 mm/m與0.2 mm/K。"],"optionsEn":["Greater total abutment thrust always improves stability regardless of its direction.","Small joint discharge proves low water pressure throughout all abutment discontinuities.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: The linear coefficients are 0.1 mm/m and 0.2 mm/K, respectively."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：線性係數分別為0.1 mm/m與0.2 mm/K。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: The linear coefficients are 0.1 mm/m and 0.2 mm/K, respectively. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b233-v15-39","title":"水溫荷載與監測殘差：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Hydrothermal effects and monitoring residuals: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b233-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「水溫荷載與監測殘差」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Hydrothermal effects and monitoring residuals” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用獨立時段驗證模型並檢查殘差隨季節和水位的結構，核對儀器更換與基準漂移；將局部裂縫、滲流與位移證據交叉比較，避免單靠統計超限下結論。將儀器更換前後的殘差分布分開檢查。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Validate on an independent period and examine residual patterns with season and level, checking instrument changes and datum drift. Cross-check cracks, seepage and movement instead of drawing conclusions from a statistical exceedance alone. Check residual distributions before and after instrument replacement as separate periods. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以水溫荷載與監測殘差編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。用獨立時段驗證模型並檢查殘差隨季節和水位的結構，核對儀器更換與基準漂移；將局部裂縫、滲流與位移證據交叉比較，避免單靠統計超限下結論。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for hydrothermal effects and monitoring residuals, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Validate on an independent period and examine residual patterns with season and level, checking instrument changes and datum drift. Cross-check cracks, seepage and movement instead of drawing conclusions from a statistical exceedance alone.","failure":"注意干擾：高度相關的水位與溫度會讓係數難以識別，模型也可能把長期損傷吸收為時間趨勢。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Correlated level and temperature make coefficients difficult to identify, and a time trend can absorb deterioration. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b233-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用獨立時段驗證模型並檢查殘差隨季節和水位的結構，核對儀器更換與基準漂移；將局部裂縫、滲流與位移證據交叉比較，避免單靠統計超限下結論。將儀器更換前後的殘差分布分開檢查。","textEn":"Validate on an independent period and examine residual patterns with season and level, checking instrument changes and datum drift. Cross-check cracks, seepage and movement instead of drawing conclusions from a statistical exceedance alone. Check residual distributions before and after instrument replacement as separate periods.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b233-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以水溫荷載與監測殘差編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。用獨立時段驗證模型並檢查殘差隨季節和水位的結構，核對儀器更換與基準漂移；將局部裂縫、滲流與位移證據交叉比較，避免單靠統計超限下結論。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for hydrothermal effects and monitoring residuals, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Validate on an independent period and examine residual patterns with season and level, checking instrument changes and datum drift. Cross-check cracks, seepage and movement instead of drawing conclusions from a statistical exceedance alone.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「水溫荷載與監測殘差」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Hydrothermal effects and monitoring residuals\"?","options":["用獨立時段驗證模型並檢查殘差隨季節和水位的結構，核對儀器更換與基準漂移；將局部裂縫、滲流與位移證據交叉比較，避免單靠統計超限下結論。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","接縫灌漿溫度只影響施工方便，不影響後續拱壩受力。"],"optionsEn":["Validate on an independent period and examine residual patterns with season and level, checking instrument changes and datum drift.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Joint-grouting temperature affects convenience only and not later arch-dam structural behavior."],"answer":0,"explanation":"用獨立時段驗證模型並檢查殘差隨季節和水位的結構，核對儀器更換與基準漂移；將局部裂縫、滲流與位移證據交叉比較，避免單靠統計超限下結論。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Validate on an independent period and examine residual patterns with season and level, checking instrument changes and datum drift. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b233-v15-40","title":"水溫荷載與監測殘差：失效診斷","titleEn":"Hydrothermal effects and monitoring residuals: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b233-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「水溫荷載與監測殘差」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Hydrothermal effects and monitoring residuals” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"高度相關的水位與溫度會讓係數難以識別，模型也可能把長期損傷吸收為時間趨勢。重新訓練前若未檢查原因，異常可能被數學上消除卻仍存在。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Correlated level and temperature make coefficients difficult to identify, and a time trend can absorb deterioration. Retraining without investigating causes may mathematically erase an anomaly while its physical source remains. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：重新訓練前若未檢查原因，異常可能被數學上消除卻仍存在。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Retraining without investigating causes may mathematically erase an anomaly while its physical source remains.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要重新擬合後殘差變小，就證明原先結構異常已消失。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A smaller residual after refitting proves the original structural anomaly has disappeared.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b233-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"高度相關的水位與溫度會讓係數難以識別，模型也可能把長期損傷吸收為時間趨勢。重新訓練前若未檢查原因，異常可能被數學上消除卻仍存在。","textEn":"Correlated level and temperature make coefficients difficult to identify, and a time trend can absorb deterioration. Retraining without investigating causes may mathematically erase an anomaly while its physical source remains.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b233-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「水溫荷載與監測殘差」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Hydrothermal effects and monitoring residuals\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","高度相關的水位與溫度會讓係數難以識別，模型也可能把長期損傷吸收為時間趨勢。","薄拱平均壓應力足夠低就證明整座雙曲拱壩沒有拉應力。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Correlated level and temperature make coefficients difficult to identify, and a time trend can absorb deterioration.","Low mean thin-arch compression proves there is no tensile stress anywhere in the dam."],"answer":1,"explanation":"高度相關的水位與溫度會讓係數難以識別，模型也可能把長期損傷吸收為時間趨勢。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Correlated level and temperature make coefficients difficult to identify, and a time trend can absorb deterioration. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-arch-2","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
